  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-100516951-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "therefore, in the present invention, the removal of contaminants is actively performed for the building drainage during the initial rainfall stage with a high content of contaminants, and some of the contaminants are considered in consideration of the low content of contaminants for the subsequent building drainage"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100584236-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "however, even with this method, it is difficult to completely remove the harmful contaminants that are strongly attached to the catchment surface by hydrophobic interaction, and the accumulated contaminants are gradually introduced into the storage tank over a long period of time during rainfall"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100584236-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "in addition, the continuous disinfection of rainwater in the storage tank requires expenditure of chemical costs, power costs, etc., and because the process is difficult to control and cumbersome, a more fundamental solution for removing the contaminants is required"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100584236-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "thus, when rainwater is concentrated on the catchment surface 2 in which contamination by contaminants is prevented early by the titanium dioxide photocatalyst layer, the rainwater is transferred to the storage tank 1 through the catchment port 3 and stored"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100614766-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "in addition, the present invention satisfactorily removes contaminants such as insecticides and herbicides contained in the drainage in the field, and suspended matters contained in the water falling out after the harrowing prior to planting, so that these suspended matters are flowed into the river or the like"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100614766-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "a discharge box (91) having an outlet partition wall (61) for storing contaminants after the contaminants are filtered and for draining the road surface dr