  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "EP-3779320-B1", "para_id": "claim_8", "text": "optionally wherein the drain blockage is determined by the controller (142) when the temperature reading of the first temperature sensor (414) is about the same as the temperature reading of the second temperature sensor (418)"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3779320-B1", "para_id": "claim_8", "text": "optionally wherein the drain blockage is determined by the controller (142) when the temperature reading of the first temperature sensor (414) is about the same as the temperature reading of the second temperature sensor (418)"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3779320-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "the controller 142 is further configured to compare the temperature readings of the first, second, and third temperature sensors 114, 118, 122 to determine whether an error has occurred in the water heater 10 (e.g., leakage, drain blockage), as further discussed below"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3779320-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "the controller 142 is further configured to compare the temperature readings of the first, second, and third temperature sensors 114, 118, 122 to determine whether an error has occurred in the water heater 10 (e.g., leakage, drain blockage), as further discussed below"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3779320-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "if the temperature of condensate is not equal to the temperature of flue gases at intermediate section 66, the controller 142 determines at box 230 that there is no drain blockage, and returns to decision point 220"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3779320-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "for example, when determining a drain blockage, the controller 142 may be configured to query the first and second temperature sensors 114, 118 during morning hours when it is most likely the user will require use of hot water"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3779320-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "for example, when determining a drain blockage, the controller 142 may be configured to query the first and second temperature sensors 114, 118 during morning hours when it is most likely the user will require use of hot water"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3779320-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "alternatively, the temperature readings of the first temperature sensor 414 during the heating mode may also be used to determine a drain blockage"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3779320-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "alternatively, the temperature readings of the first temperature sensor 414 during the heating mode may also be used to determine a drain blockage"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3779320-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "in particular, when the temperature readings of the first temperature sensor 414 decrease toward the minimum temperature limit 682 during the heating mode, the controller will determine that there is a drain blockage"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3779320-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "in particular, when the temperature readings of the first temperature sensor 414 decrease toward the minimum temperature limit 682 during the heating mode, the controller will determine that there is a drain blockage"}, {"pat_id": "US-10184221-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "for example, low temperature conditions may indicate ice formation which could prevent water control by blockage of water through the drains of the water control devices"}]</data>
</edge>
