  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-101611632-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "as water and water vapor pass through each of the sub-chambers of the vessel 12, additional water vapor is produced and the temperature of the water vapor is raised to leave salt, dissolved solids, and other contaminants in the remaining water"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101828136-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "as water and water vapor pass through each of the lower chambers of the vessel 12, the temperature of the water vapor is increased to produce additional water vapor, leaving salts, dissolved solids and other contaminants in the remaining water"}, {"pat_id": "US-4659347-A", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "thus, the method according to my invention comprises the steps of (a) emitting the water in one or more jets into a vessel maintained under a pressure low enough to let part of that water be vaporized--together with accompanying contaminants--at an ambient temperature, preferably at or below the usual room temperature of about 20 -25 c."}, {"pat_id": "US-9102545-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "as the water and water vapor passes through each subchamber of the vessel 12, the temperature of the water vapor is increased such that additional water vapor is created and leaves the salts, dissolved solids, and other contaminants behind in the remaining water"}]</data>
