  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "EP-0527545-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "as the ambient temperature has dropped to about 5 c or below, the first valve is heated by a heater in which it is housed, thereby preventing its freezing"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3983776-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "for example, the smart water valve 126 can determine that the temperature of the water leak of 60 degrees f matches the temperature of water consumed by the toilet of 177 degrees c (62 degrees f)"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3983776-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "in some examples, the smart water valve 126 can determine that temperature of the water leak matches the temperature of the particular water consuming device based on the temperatures matching within a threshold variance"}, {"pat_id": "JP-S5851260-Y2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "an anti-freeze valve 2 (low-temperature valve) connected to piping 1 is used to prevent freezing by lowering the water temperature to a temperature equal to or close to that of the water"}, {"pat_id": "KR-0175895-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "four-way valve driving means for driving control of the four-way valve to prevent freezing of the cold water tank, it is characterized in that the compressor driving means for controlling the drive to increase the temperature of the cold water tank according to the control to prevent freezing of the cold water tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100908201-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in the sludge preventing and freezing prevention apparatus of the present invention installed as described above, when the temperature of the water is lower than the predetermined temperature, the water supply pipe 20 is opened by the operation of the high pressure pump 30 while the water supply pipe 10 is opened with the automatic opening and closing valve 50"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100991888-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in order to prevent freezing of the water supply pipe, the water supply valve was opened slightly so that the water flow was always maintained in the water supply pipe so that water was always circulated in the water supply pipe, or a separate heat radiator was installed to increase the temperature of the water supply pipe"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100991888-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "thus, the controller c opens the first opening / closing valve v\u2081 and simultaneously shuts off the second opening / closing valve v2 when the temperature sensor 13 detects the expected temperature of the freezing wave"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101194416-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "another object of the present invention is to maintain the temperature of the fluid through the housing provided in the first double pipe, the second double pipe, the valve meets each other, and to prevent the freezing of the water pipe to prevent freezing of the water pipe in winter to provide a structure"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101194416-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "second, since the portions where the first double pipe 110, the second double pipe 120, and the valve 130 meet each other are covered by the accommodation housing 140, the temperature of the fluid and the freezing of the water pipe in winter are prevented"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101194416-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in addition, since the portions where the first double pipe 110, the second double pipe 120, and the valve 130 meet each other are covered by the accommodation housing 140, the temperature of the fluid and the freezing of the water pipe in winter are prevented"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101203179-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "second, since portions where the first double pipe, the second double pipe, and the valve meet each other are covered by the housing, it is possible to prevent the freezing of the water pipe during the winter as well as maintaining the temperature of the fluid"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101289929-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "as another example, the controller 14 may receive the temperature of the water in the water pipe detected by the temperature detection sensor unit 11, and block the valve 13 when the temperature of the water in the water pipe rises above a predetermined temperature"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101289929-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "that is, the controller 14 confirms that the temperature rises within the reference temperature range during the first reference time interval while the temperature of the water in the water pipe is falling, thereby opening the valve to prevent freezing, or the temperature of the water in the water pipe is reduced"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101289929-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "2 if the temperature is kept constant below the second preset reference temperature during the reference time interval, two freezing determination techniques for opening the valve to prevent freezing may be applied"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101356118-B1", "para_id": "claim_3", "text": "groundwater upper protection ball safety device, characterized in that to prevent the freezing of the water pipe 20 by opening the automatic discharge valve (50) when the temperature is reached by setting the temperature"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101665052-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "[0001] apparatus for preventing frozen of water [0002]the present invention relates to a freeze prevention device, and more particularly, to a freeze prevention device that is installed in a facility related to the use of water such as a faucet, a water pipe, or a meter to prevent freezing of water and adjust the opening temperature of the valve"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102300746-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "as such, in the water pipe freezing prevention system according to the embodiment of the present invention, the opening timing and opening amount of the electromagnetic valve 3 installed in the water pipe 2 are automatically controlled through the controller 10 of the boiler 1 according to the external temperature"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102440380-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "however, in the case of a freeze prevention module equipped with such a temperature-type automatic valve, the temperature is measured to prevent freezing through heat transfer, but if the module is exposed to sub-zero weather for a long time, abnormal operation may be executed"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102440380-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "this is because when the temperature drops to sub-zero range in winter, rupture due to freezing in valves or pipes may occur"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102467167-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the present invention relates to a water valve for preventing freezing of a water pipe to prevent freezing of a water pipe by discharging water little by little as the stem holder operates and a waterway is partially opened when the temperature is lowered"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102467167-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "however, in the case of a water valve located outdoors, it is difficult to use the water pipe or the tap water inside the water valve due to the freezing temperature in winter, and the volume expansion of the frozen tap water causes the water pipe or the connection parts of the water pipe to deteriorate"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102467167-B1", "para_id": "para_4", "text": "in order to prevent freezing of tap water, conventionally, a method of warming the water valve and the water pipe by wrapping the surroundings of the water valve and the water pipe with a heat insulating material has been most widely used, but the effect is insufficient when the temperature drops significantly"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102512635-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the automatic dripping device 100 for freezing prevention according to the present embodiment may open and close the on/off valve 140 by a specific angle according to the temperature data obtained from the temperature detector 120"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102512635-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the power supply unit 170 may provide power stored therein to the temperature detection unit 120, the control unit 130, and the opening/closing valve driving unit when the power supplied from the outside to the automatic dripping device 100 for preventing freezing is cut off"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102572857-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "another method for preventing the water pipe from freezing is to prevent the water pipe from freezing by artificially opening a water valve to continuously drain the water when it is expected that the water contained in the water pipe will freeze due to low temperature"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102587945-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "additionally, it is possible to prevent freezing of the air valve 90 in a convenient and effective manner by configuring the heating element 44, solar cell 55, temperature sensor, signal transmitter, and control unit"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102600404-B1", "para_id": "para_8", "text": "therefore, when the temperature drops, such as in the winter, freezing due to residual water inside the flow path is inevitable, and when freezing occurs, the entire water angle valve must be replaced, which inevitably results in excessive costs"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200309420-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in order to solve the above problems, a heating freeze protection device has been proposed, which installs a separate heater around the valve and the pipe to prevent freezing by heating the pipe when the ambient temperature drops"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200426270-Y1", "para_id": "claim_2", "text": "the method of claim 1, by measuring the temperature of the water by the temperature sensor 5 in the water pipe (p2), when the temperature is less than the set temperature, the inlet valve 7 and the outlet valve 19 for a predetermined time to prevent freezing by circulation of water secondary water purification equipment"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200426270-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "and, the flow sensor to prevent the freezing of the filter and the device by opening the inlet valve 7 and outlet valve 19 for a predetermined time when the temperature sensor (5) located in the water pipe (p2) below a set temperature"}, {"pat_id": "US-10046988-B2", "para_id": "para_28", "text": "a blocking valve is advantageously inserted at the filtrate outlet of the filter which stops the permeate flow to the place of use in the event of deviation from predetermined trend data or in the event of defective process data, such as defective conductivity and/or temperature"}, {"pat_id": "US-10989621-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in other words, in such embodiments, fluidly connecting an upstream sensor 58a to a vent port 42 on a pipe fitting 18 may include fluidly connecting a fluid temperature sensor 58 between the vent port 42 and a fluid valve 60 in the testing apparatus 40, for example, via one or more external fluid conduits 62, such as a hose (process block 98)"}, {"pat_id": "US-11066813-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in some example embodiments, the system may receive weather data, and if there is prediction of sub-zero temperatures in the forecast, the system may automatically turn on the main valve to allow water to flow through the pipes, thereby preventing the pipe from freezing"}, {"pat_id": "US-11066813-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "when the temperature drops, the system opens the main valve and allows the water to flow, thus preventing the pipe from freezing"}, {"pat_id": "US-11325845-B2", "para_id": "para_4", "text": "a blowdown temperature control loop may be initialized and an extra source valve command cap may be determined in block 8018 as well"}, {"pat_id": "US-11352267-B2", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "a blowdown temperature control loop may be initialized and an extra source valve command cap may be determined in block 8018 as well"}, {"pat_id": "US-12385572-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in another embodiment, the present valve is connected to the control system and includes remote sensors for monitoring temperature, leaks, water flow and the like, which are installed in other areas of the house and are configured for communicating with the main control system and the valve"}, {"pat_id": "US-4456024-A", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "ambient temperatures below freezing but of insufficient duration to reduce the water temperature to the freezing point, will not activate the valve resulting in an unnecessary discharge of water"}, {"pat_id": "US-4672990-A", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "despite colder above-ground ambient temperatures, radiant heat from main water supply line 2 should prevent freezing of main branch line 3 and main valve 4"}, {"pat_id": "US-4763682-A", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the valve closing element of this patent is caused to open said valve and allow the drainage of fluid from a connected pipe in response to temperatures approaching the freezing point"}, {"pat_id": "US-4763682-A", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "it is therefore seen that the present invention provides a simple device for activating a fluid valve in response to a thermal, and specifically, to a freezing, change in temperature, without the requirement for external power or human intervention"}, {"pat_id": "US-4784173-A", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "after the valve has been opened to bleed water from the water line, it thereafter closes because of such heat transfer and is again in position to operate responsively to freezing ambient temperatures"}, {"pat_id": "US-4784173-A", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "when freezing temperatures are sensed by the bulb, there is an outflow of water from the valve device and an inflow of water from the inlet conduit, thereby preventing freezing of water within the tank"}, {"pat_id": "US-4784173-A", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "thus, there is a need for a completely failure-safe freeze prevention valve that is useful under industrial conditions, automatically responsive to freezing temperatures and to thawing temperatures, completely reliable as a standby device, entirely independent of outside power sources, incapable of leaking, and operable without periodic maintenance"}, {"pat_id": "US-4798239-A", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the two anti-freezing valves 15 and 16 effectively protect the meter against freezing by virtue of the transfer of heat from soil zones where the collectors 10 are buried, to the valves 15 and 16 flanking the meter, thereby preventing the freezing of the water circulating from the valve 15 to the valve 16, even in the case of a substantially negative temperature of the adjacent atmosphere"}, {"pat_id": "US-5715855-A", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the temperature of household water, continuously flowing through to the outdoor valves, is usually sufficient to prevent freezing of the valve and associated plumbing"}, {"pat_id": "US-5715855-A", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "description of the invention brief summary of the invention the present invention provides a simple design for a mechanically actuated, temperature-responsive valve that efficiently utilizes the volumetric expansion of freezing water to cause water from an outdoor tap to flow through discharge ports"}, {"pat_id": "US-5876596-A", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "after valve 44 has been open for a sufficiently long interval to permit the essentially deuterium free water from separator 28 to flow into tank 50, timer 62 or microprocessor 18 activates cooling element 56 to reduce the temperature of the water sample to the freezing point (32 f.)"}, {"pat_id": "US-6003780-A", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "interruption of water supply pressure, when the main fountain valve 20 is in the off condition, does not result in exposing any portion of the collected water to freezing temperatures"}, {"pat_id": "US-6021798-A", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "when the temperature rises above freezing, the sensor is de-actuated to interrupt the flow of electricity from the power source to the solenoid-actuated valve, and thereby close the valve and stop the flow of water therethrough"}, {"pat_id": "US-6182453-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "including the peltier probe itself can be activated in reverse, to provide a sufficient amount of heating to prevent freezing of the lines, valves, and reservoir when the ambient or housing panel temperature falls into the range 5 to 5 c"}, {"pat_id": "US-6763845-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "indeed, in some particularly preferred embodiments of this invention, the third valve may be attached to a water utilization device that is located out of doors and therefore exposed to freezing temperatures"}, {"pat_id": "US-7497228-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "because the temperature control valve measured a higher temperature, it would remain closed and not allow warmer water from below ground to replace the freezing water"}, {"pat_id": "US-9238904-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the temperature sensing device detects the temperature of the fluid within the flushing device 100, measuring for freezing conditions, and triggers the freeze control valve 710 to open under predetermined temperatures, such as freezing condition temperatures, to prevent freezing of the fluid within the flushing device 100"}, {"pat_id": "US-9752787-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the drain pipe allows for any water that may build up in, or leak into, the valve box to drain away before it can change to steam under the high temperature conditions and cause damage"}]</data>
</edge>
