ight of the weight 123 of the lever valve 120 to the original position, the valve surface 122 can block the drain groove 141 to prevent the introduction of various wastes (fig"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100672275-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "2, the general operation of the rainwater toss is usually performed by sliding the valve valve plate 17 to the lower guide block 27 of the torsion housing 1 by the operation of the drive motor 19"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100699326-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "and, the connecting valve 42 is a manure to prevent the failure of the device due to the pinch of the foreign matter caught in the bent portion of the connecting pipe 41 when the role of water purification and water purification is not made smoothly, it is configured to control inflow and block rainwater"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100706162-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "when rainwater is introduced through the manhole cover 30 while the installation is completed as described above, the introduced rainwater is introduced into the odor blocking tube 110, and the rainwater is opened while the elastic valve 115 is opened by the load of the rainwater"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100706162-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "on the other hand, the elastic valve 115 is closed when all the rain water is discharged, the weight 111 of the odor blocking tube 110 when the elastic valve 115 is closed at all times the lowest level of sewage flowing through the inside of the manhole body 10 odor is blocked because it is located less than the discharge of the manhole cover"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101275666-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in addition, on one side of the sump (1), in addition to the blocking of the odor, the reverse valve (7) for preventing the reverse flow is axially coupled to the hinge shaft (8) inclined axially configured to prevent odor or reverse flow while allowing drainage do"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101537963-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the valve 320 blocks the inflow of rainwater when the filter 331 installed in the filter housing 330 is exchanged, thereby facilitating a smooth filter replacement operation"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101771073-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the valve 31 rises above the inflow section 21 of the rainwater infiltration pipe 20 to open the inflow section 21 and contrarily to the lower side of the inflow section 21 to close the inflow section 21, the structured inflow part 21 is not closed but the space between the inflow part 21 and the discharge part 22 is blocked to prevent the rainwater flowing through the inflow part 21 from flowing to the discharge part 22"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102216793-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "as described above, after removing the collecting plate 28 and the sensor 25, when the handle 29 of the top tank 12 is lifted and lifted, the inlet of the lower tank 12 from the drain 19 of the upper tank 12 as (18) is separated, the open upper tank valve 12 is closed, so that rainwater in the upper tank 12 can be prevented from leaking"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200328170-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "it is possible to install a larger number of valves in a limited area of the lid to provide a sewage odor blocking device that can lead to the sewage pipe in a faster time when a large amount of sewage or rainwater is generated"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200361466-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "it has been disclosed that the odor blocking device of the rainwater receiver has a long oval structure so that sludge components contained in rainwater or sewage do not accumulate in the discharge end of the valve body"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200403906-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in such a state, when rainwater flows instantaneously, when the rainwater is instantaneously introduced, the floats 40 are raised to block the inlet 12 of the buoy automatic shutoff valve body 10 due to the disk 20, and the sewage and rainwater are sewage"}]</data>
