  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "EP-0576981-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "the sensor 51 also gives the possibility that when the water level in the washing chamber 21 drops, for example due to leakage losses, the vacuum blower 36 can be switched on again in order to compensate for these leakage losses and to always have a fully filled washing chamber available for washing processes"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3779320-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "the wait period 695 ends when the leaking water has reached a predetermined water level in the drain pipe 394, and the leaking water is then able to exit through the drain line 398 past the first temperature sensor 414"}, {"pat_id": "JP-2780720-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "that is, when the water level of the pair of water level sensors installed in the snow channel changes, the blockage of the two water level sensors is determined by judging which of the three types of the fluctuations is the above-described pattern"}, {"pat_id": "JP-2780720-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "that is, when the water level of the pair of water level sensors installed in the snow channel changes, the blockage of the two water level sensors is determined by judging which of the three types of the fluctuations is the above-described pattern"}, {"pat_id": "JP-2780720-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in addition, since fluctuations in the water level are also observed in other water level monitoring panels in the system, the overall system determines the blockage position in units of sections where water level sensors are installed by comprehensively judging the detection results of each water level monitoring panel"}, {"pat_id": "JP-2780720-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in addition, since fluctuations in the water level are also observed in other water level monitoring panels in the system, the overall system determines the blockage position in units of sections where water level sensors are installed by comprehensively judging the detection results of each water level monitoring panel"}, {"pat_id": "JP-2780720-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "also, in consideration of the degree of water level difference between the two points, the absolute water level of each water level sensor, etc., the urgency of the water level rise due to blockage is divided into, for example, three stages, and only the alarm lamp is turned on in the first stage"}, {"pat_id": "JP-2780720-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "also, in consideration of the degree of water level difference between the two points, the absolute water level of each water level sensor, etc., the urgency of the water level rise due to blockage is divided into, for example, three stages, and only the alarm lamp is turned on in the first stage"}, {"pat_id": "JP-7183463-B1", "para_id": "para_40", "text": "for example, the monitoring device 200 uses the measurement data of the sensor devices 210 distributed in the a block to calculate the dynamic water level at each location in the a block"}, {"pat_id": "JP-7183463-B1", "para_id": "para_119", "text": "in step s1520, the water leakage detection system 20 calculates the time-series dynamic water level at each monitoring location (installation location of each sensor device 210)"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100510269-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "into the flow rate adjustment tank 30 in a state in which the coarse contaminant is filtered and removed while passing through), and when the water level detection sensor 33 of the flow adjustment tank 30 detects the water level, the raw water pump 31 according to the detected signal"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100546851-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in the control unit 90, when the second filter material 22a of the second filter tank 20 is blocked and the water level is increased, the water flows back through the overflow pipe 45, and this is applied to the detection signal of the second water level sensor 22b"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100546851-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the control unit 90 is blocked by the second filter material 22a of the second filter tank 20 when the water level is increased, the water flows back through the overflow pipe 45, by the detection signal of the second water level sensor 22b the operation of the inflow pump 70 is stopped"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100720388-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "at this time, the primary electrolysis panel unit 100 is provided with a level sensor 111 for measuring the water level of the brine tank (110a), while opening and closing the solenoid valve 112 in accordance with the set water level to replenish the time a first water level detecting unit 110"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100841664-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "the fifth water level sensor 45 detects an overflow phenomenon that occurs when the water level in the electrolytic cell 30 is increased due to a blockage of the outlet 27a or the like, which is not drained or an increase in inflow from the storage tank 20"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100932027-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in particular, the temporary storage tank of chemicals is formed by double walls of the outer wall and the inner wall so that even if the chemical exceeds the inner wall due to the malfunction of the water level control valve, it is protected by the outer wall as well as between the inner wall and the outer wall, that is, the leak detection sensor installed in the safety space"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100932027-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in particular, the temporary storage tank of chemicals is formed by double walls of the outer wall and the inner wall, so that even if the chemical exceeds the inner wall due to the malfunction of the automatic water level control valve, it is protected by the outer wall, and between the inner wall and the outer wall, that is, a leak detection sensor installed in the safety space"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100985209-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "as a result, the reliability of controlling the water level of the water tank can