: "US-11325845-B2", "para_id": "para_4", "text": "in some embodiments, the individual derivatives determined from each product temperature sensor 6082a-d may all be required to be less than the threshold in order for the controller 6034 to proceed to block 7840"}, {"pat_id": "US-11325845-B2", "para_id": "para_4", "text": "in some embodiments, if any of the individual derivatives determined from each product temperature sensor 6082a-d are less than the threshold, the controller 6034 may proceed to block 7844"}, {"pat_id": "US-11352267-B2", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "if, in block 7348, the difference for each is greater than a threshold set for each respective parameter, the controller 6034 calculates a derivative based on data received from at least one temperature sensor in the system 6000 in block 7351"}, {"pat_id": "US-11352267-B2", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "for example, the controller 6034 may calculate a derivative based on data received from a low pressure steam temperature sensor 6066 in block 7351"}, {"pat_id": "US-11352267-B2", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "otherwise, the controller 6034 may, in block 7392, receive temperature data signals from one or more product temperature sensor (e.g"}, {"pat_id": "US-11352267-B2", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "if, at block 7069, the system 6000 is currently in a normal water production mode, the target temperature 7068 along with a product or condensate output temperature 7070 determined from data provided by a product output sensor (e.g"}, {"pat_id": "US-11352267-B2", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "a current low pressure steam temperature may be received by the controller 6034 in block 6884 from, for example, a low pressure steam temperature sensor 6066 (see, e.g., fig"}, {"pat_id": "US-11352267-B2", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "in block 7528, the controller 6034 may receive data from each of the product temperature sensors (e.g"}, {"pat_id": "US-11352267-B2", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "in block 7832, the controller 6034 may find a derivate of the product level based on data received from the product temperature sensor(s) 6082a-d"}, {"pat_id": "US-11352267-B2", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "in some embodiments, the individual derivatives determined from each product temperature sensor 6082a-d may all be required to be less than the threshold in order for the controller 6034 to proceed to block 7840"}, {"pat_id": "US-11352267-B2", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "in some embodiments, if any of the individual derivatives determined from each product temperature sensor 6082a-d are less than the threshold, the controller 6034 may proceed to block 7844"}, {"pat_id": "US-11549837-B2", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "thus, a single set of localized sensors (flow rate sensor 105, optional pressure sensor 65, optional acoustic sensor, and/or optional temperature sensor 93) can be utilized and incorporated into the water meter and leak detection system 10 (126 shown in figs"}, {"pat_id": "US-11549837-B2", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "thus, a single set of localized sensors (flow rate sensor 105, optional pressure sensor 65, optional acoustic sensor, and/or optional temperature sensor 93) can be utilized and incorporated into the water meter and leak detection system 10 (126 shown in figs"}, {"pat_id": "US-11549837-B2", "para_id": "para_4", "text": "for measuring or monitoring the temperature of the water flowing through the water meter and leak detection system 10, 126, the use of various thermocouples or thermistor sensors 70 as depicted in fig"}, {"pat_id": "US-11549837-B2", "para_id": "para_4", "text": "for measuring or monitoring the temperature of the water flowing through the water meter and leak detection system 10, 126, the use of various thermocouples or thermistor sensors 70 as depicted in fig"}, {"pat_id": "US-11608618-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in an alternative embodiment, the addition of an external environment sensor probe and temperature sensor package to a leak detection system creates a more comprehensive system able to prevent and detect leaks"}, {"pat_id": "US-11608618-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in an alternative embodiment, the addition of an external environment sensor probe and temperature sensor package to a leak detection system creates a more comprehensive system able to prevent and detect leaks"}, {"pat_id": "US-11608618-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in an alternative embodiment of the invention, a temperature sensor and a heating element is utilized to detect fluid flow rate of a system, detect fluid leaks of a system, to detect fluid temperature, and to prevent fluid freeze conditions"}, {"pat_id": "US-11608618-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in addition, the primary temperature sensor package 702 and the secondary temperature sensor package 706 may be utilized to raise the temperature of the fluid to prevent the fluid within the fluid conduit system 720 from freezing"}, {"pat_id": "US-11608618-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in addition, the primary temperature sensor package 806 and the secondary temperature sensor package 840 may be utilized to raise the temperature of the fluid to prevent the fluid within the fluid conduit system 810 from freezing"}, {"pat_id": "US-11814821-B2", "para_id": "claim_2", "text": "and a leak detector controller in communication with said first sensor and said second sensor configured to sense said ambient temperature from said first sensor and generating said drive signal to drive said second sensor to said elevated temperature greater than said ambient temperature and to generate a leak signal when said drive signal of said second sensor exceeds a leak point value"}, {"pat_id": "US-11814821-B2", "para_id": "claim_18", "text": "and a leak detector controller in communication with said first sensor and said second sensor configured to sense said ambient temperature from said first sensor and generating said drive signal to drive said second sensor to said elevated temperature greater than said ambient temperature and to generate said leak condition when said drive signal of said second sensor exceeds a leak point value"}, {"pat_id": "US-11814821-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in an alternative embodiment, the addition of an external environment sensor probe and temperature sensor package to a leak detection system creates a more comprehensive system able to prevent and detect leaks"}, {"pat_id": "US-11814821-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in an alternative embodiment, the addition of an external environment sensor probe and temperature sensor package to a leak detection system creates a more comprehensive system able to prevent and detect leaks"}, {"pat_id": "US-11905688-B2", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "a water device with a pressure, temperature and/or flow sensor coupled to the fluid in a pipe or the plumbing system is affected by egress, flow, leaks, and use in the municipal water system"}, {"pat_id": "US-11998860-B2", "para_id": "para_17", "text": "if the air temperature sensor 140 is activated, the system 100 will stop operations due to an inability of the air heater with fan 143 to raise the produced water or wastewater temperature in the sump (bottom) of the container 139, 339 above the freezing point"}, {"pat_id": "US-12163944-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "temperature sensors traditionally used within the industry are of resistive temperature detector (rtd) type, and are typically configured with a stainless steel dome to prevent malfunction due to corrosion and water ingress issues"}, {"pat_id": "US-12337259-B2", "para_id": "para_25", "text": "if the air temperature sensor 140 is activated, the system 100 will stop operations due to an inability of the air heater with fan 143 to raise the wastewater temperature in the sump (bottom) of the container 139, 339 above the freezing point"}, {"pat_id": "US-12385572-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in another embodiment, the present valve is connected to the control system and includes remote sensors for monitoring temperature, leaks, water flow and the like, which are installed in other areas of the house and are configured for communicating with the main control system and the valve"}, {"pat_id": "US-5638847-A", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "moreover, the moisture and temperature sensors may not be positioned to detect a leak, for incipient freeze condition, and thus, the flow sensor would provide the last line of defense to water damage"}, {"pat_id": "US-6021798-A", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "when the temperature rises above freezing, the sensor is de-actuated to interrupt the flow of electricity from the power source to the solenoid-actuated valve, and thereby close the valve and stop the flow of water therethrough"}, {"pat_id": "US-6436299-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the ambient temperature sensor circuit measures the ambient temperature of the atmosphere, so that the water treatment system can maintain a temperature level above freezing or some other predetermined temperature"}, {"pat_id": "US-6436299-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the ambient temperature sensor circuit 114 measures the ambient temperature of the atmosphere so that the water treatment system 10 can maintain a temperature level above freezing or some other predetermined temperature setting"}, {"pat_id": "US-6441618-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "it is a further aspect of the present invention to implement the aforementioned monitoring step by utilizing sensors which have been used in the oil industry, such as the sensors used for general reservoir monitoring, and/or the sensors used for leak detection, soil heating, and temperature mapping"}, {"pat_id": "US-6441618-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the sensors used for general reservoir monitoring that are disclosed in the first reference cited above, and/or the sensors used for leak detection, soil heating, and temperature mapping that are disclosed in the second set of references cited above"}, {"pat_id": "US-7549435-B2", "para_id": "para_51", "text": "in such a configuration, a sensor, such as a temperature sensor, may be included to determine the source of a particular leak among one of a plurality of fluid sources"}, {"pat_id": "US-9534978-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in an alternative embodiment, the addition of an external environment sensor probe and temperature sensor package to a leak detection system creates a more comprehensive system able to prevent and detect leaks"}, {"pat_id": "US-9534978-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in an alternative embodiment, the addition of an external environment sensor probe and temperature sensor package to a leak detection system creates a more comprehensive system able to prevent and detect leaks"}]</data>
