introduced into the rainwater chamber 10 is increased in quantity and gradually increased in water level to reach the moving induction plate 300 installed in the sewage inlet 22 and the blocking plate 260"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101258565-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the rainwater introduced into the rainwater chamber 10 is increased in quantity and gradually increased in water level to reach the moving induction plate 300 installed in the sewage inlet 22 and the blocking plate 260"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101323649-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "first, if rainwater is supplied through the inlet 1 of the single finishing block 20, it is stored while maintaining the same water level in the entire pipeline while flowing along the curved pipe"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101388033-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "when the water level of the sewage stored in the tank 30 rises and the height of the buckle member 54 increases, the wire 56b is pulled up by the load of the sensing block 56c and the sensing block 56c is lowered"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101388033-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "if the water level of the sewage is continuously increased, the bure member 54 is raised and the sensing block 56c is lowered, so that the sensing block 56c is the fourth contact sensor 58d, the third contact sensor 58c, and the second"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101439225-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in this case, as the water level l measured by the water level sensor 31 increases or decreases, the amount of the contaminants blocked by the screen member also increases or decreases proportionally to the internal water"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101588396-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "on the other hand, when the float valve 16 is closed by the buoy 17, the water level of the dirt increases due to the dirt that flows into the dirt collection vehicle, thereby blocking the movement of the air and further preventing the dirt from being introduced into the collection vehicle"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101996050-B1", "para_