ized in that the anti-pollution cap is configured to be coupled to the upper side of the casing to support the water level sensor to prevent contaminants from entering the ground"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101311288-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the drainage pump is provided with a water level sensor to drain the stagnant water while the position of the sediment detector descends to the settled contaminant surface"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101311288-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the drainage pump is provided with a water level sensor to drain the stagnant water while the position of the sediment detector descends to the settled contaminant surface"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101322190-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "therefore, when the purified treatment water from which the contaminants have been removed through the purification treatment water recovery pipe 140 provided in the internal treatment tank 200 of the present invention is recovered, the amount corresponding to the purification treatment water by the water level detection means and the control unit 600"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101439225-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in this case, as the water level l measured by the water level sensor 31 increases or decreases, the amount of the contaminants blocked by the screen member also increases or decreases proportionally to the internal water"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101741449-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "that is, if the operating time of the filtration tank is increased, the flow rate of the flow of the rainwater or the flow rate of the treated water is lowered due to the increase of the amount of contaminants collected in the lcd artificial floating filter media, or the water level of the tank before the rainwater is increased do"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200323476-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "into the flow rate adjustment tank 30 in a state in which the coarse contaminant is filtered and removed while passing through), and when the water level detection sensor 33 of the flow adjustment tank 30 detects the water level, the raw water pump 31 according to the detected signal"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200323476-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "into the flow rate adjustment tank 30 in a state in which the coarse contaminant is filtered and removed while passing through), and when the water level detection sensor 33 of the flow adjustment tank 30 detects the water level, the raw water pump 31 according to the detected signal"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200323476-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "into the flow rate adjustment tank 30 in a state in which the coarse contaminant is filtered and removed while passing through), and when the water level detection sensor 33 of the flow adjustment tank 30 detects the water level, the raw water pump 31 according to the detected signal"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200326076-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "since the second filtration system 40 is relatively small and runs for a long time, it filters out contaminants as much as possible, enters the filtered water into the water level control tank 10 and consequently returns it to the swimming pool"}]</data>
