  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "EP-3309310-B1", "para_id": "claim_7", "text": "rain overflow tank (1) according to at least one of the preceding claims, characterized in that a sensor device is provided and the degree of contamination of the retaining element (11) can be derived from the measurement data of the sensor device"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3466513-B1", "para_id": "claim_7", "text": "rain overflow tank (1) according to at least one of the preceding claims, characterized in that at least one sensor device (18a, 18b) is provided, and the degree of contamination of the retaining elements (8, 22) is derived from the measurement data of the sensor device (18a, 18b), preferably from the measurement data of two sensor devices (18a, 18b)"}, {"pat_id": "JP-4029133-B2", "para_id": "para_6", "text": "it is possible to prevent the water in the water storage tank 2 from leaking, and it is possible to surely switch between water storage and water discharge by opening and closing the drain hole 11c with the drain hole opening / closing lid 13"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100350735-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "however, during rainfall, the amount of sewage inflow is high and the flow rate is fast, so that the soil is not deposited in the sedimentation tank and flows into the dwelling house as it is, so that the cross section of the dwelling house 3 is reduced and the sewage terminal treatment plant is caused"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100549466-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "cylindrical filter 40 is connected to the supply pipe 30 to clean the primary filtered rainwater from the water tank 21 to filter impurities or organic matter, so that the rainwater stored in the water tank 10 is decayed by eutrophication or it is possible to prevent the end of deterioration and the like"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100584236-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "however, even with this method, it is difficult to completely remove the harmful contaminants that are strongly attached to the catchment surface by hydrophobic interaction, and the accumulated contaminants are gradually introduced into the storage tank over a long period of time during rainfall"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100584236-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "in addition, the continuous disinfection of rainwater in the storage tank requires expenditure of chemical costs, power costs, etc., and because the process is difficult to control and cumbersome, a more fundamental solution for removing the contaminants is required"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100584236-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "thus, when rainwater is concentrated on the catchment surface 2 in which contamination by contaminants is prevented early by the titanium dioxide photocatalyst layer, the rainwater is transferred to the storage tank 1 through the catchment port 3 and stored"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100584236-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "thus, when rainwater is concentrated on the catchment surface 2 in which contamination by contaminants is prevented early by the titanium dioxide photocatalyst layer, the rainwater is transferred to the storage tank 1 through the catchment port 3 and stored"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100614766-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "the treated water through which the contaminant is removed by passing through the filter medium filling tank 71 is accommodated in the discharge box 91 by overflowing through the discharge unit 90, and then introduced into the drain pipe or artificial wetland through the drainage path 100"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100614766-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "therefore, in the present invention, the removal of contaminants is actively performed on the road drainage during the initial rainfall stage in which the content of the pollutants is high, and the filter filling tank 71 considering the low amount of pollutants in the subsequent road drainage"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100614766-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "in addition, the removal process of pollutants deposited on the road surface is almost completed in the initial rainfall stage, and since the amount of pollutants in the road drainage due to the subsequent rainfall remains small, the road drainage does not come into contact with the media installed in the treatment tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100614766-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "(3) since the filter filling tank which removes contaminants contained in the drainage by filtration or adsorption is detachably installed in the treatment tank, while the drainage flowed from the inlet of the storm receiver flows through the treatment tank, contaminants contained in the waste water are removed by the filter medium"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100660052-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "because of this, the block body 30 is installed in a row arrangement of the role of the storage tank for storing rainwater and the waterway line is formed so that the concentrated phenomenon does not occur even in a large amount of rain"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100702860-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in addition, in the excellent storage tank of the present invention, by forming the outer wall block and the storage block in the hexahedral structure with the upper and lower sides open while the opening is formed as described above, compared to the storage block of the conventional hexahedral structure with the upper and lower plates closed, the raw material cost is reduced along with this, there is another purpose of making the outer wall block and the storage block and the construction of the rainwater storage tank through the block very easy"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100702860-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "at this time, in the case of the outer wall block (10, 10a) the inner wall of the storage tank (1) to achieve the outer wall of the storage tank (1) while smoothly flowing with the prevention of leakage of rainwater moved from each storage block (20)"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100702860-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "at this time, in the case of the outer wall block (10, 10a) the inner wall of the storage tank (1) to achieve the outer wall of the storage tank (1) while smoothly flowing with the prevention of leakage of rainwater moved from each storage block (20)"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100750645-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "it is provided in the storage space of the treatment tank 6 includes a filtration device (9) for filtering and adsorption to remove contaminants contained in the road surface drainage rising from the lower portion of the treatment tank (6)"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100750645-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "therefore, the amount of contaminants in the road surface drainage due to the subsequent rainfall is small, and it can be said that there is little problem even if the excess water is discharged immediately without passing through the filtration tank 54"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100752792-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "subsequently, the amount of rainwater transferred to the flow regulating tank 3 is controlled to increase rapidly, and a certain amount of air is supplied through an diffuser installed at the bottom of the flow regulating tank 3 to prevent sedimentation and decay of the sludge"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100784496-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the filtration tank 30 is provided with a filter 31 for filtering contaminants such as organic substances, oil components, and suspended solids in the rainfall that do not settle in the precipitation tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100784496-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in addition, the contaminants having their own weight among the contaminants included in the initial rainfall introduced into the first settling tank 10 are primarily precipitated at the bottom of the first settling tank 10 and do not settle in the first settling tank 10"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100784496-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "meanwhile, contaminants having their own weight among the pollutants included in the rainfall flowing into the second settling tank 20 are second precipitated to the bottom of the second settling tank 20"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100784496-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in addition, regardless of the heavy rain or heavy rain, the initial rainfall is necessarily passed through the purification tank, it is possible to prevent the contamination of the river by the initial rainfall"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100786511-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "this phenomenon causes a vortex phenomenon while the rainwater including the pollutant moving in the contaminant treatment tank 13 passes through the rainwater port 16 eccentrically to one side, and despite this vortex phenomenon, 17) and the reverse flow prevention plate 18 once settles down as it is"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100786511-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "fine suspended matter having little specific gravity remaining after being precipitated in the contaminant treatment tank 13 is moved through the filter 20 installed in the upper part to the storm conduit 12 due to the continuous inflow of rainwater"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100792022-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "an index member 33 made of a general rubber material or a synthetic resin material is installed to prevent leakage of rainwater stored from the water storage tank 1 having a horizontally sealed structure"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100819522-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "an index member 33 made of a general rubber material or a synthetic resin material is installed to prevent leakage of rainwater stored from the water storage tank 1 having a horizontally sealed structure"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100823240-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "therefore, when the initial rainwater and sediment contaminants are completely excluded from the initial rainwater treatment facility 1 and the pressure or water level becomes zero, the drain pump 21 receiving the water is driven to operate the water tank 10"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100927631-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "at this time, when rainwater flows into the sedimentation tank 200, heavy foreign matter such as sand sinks to the bottom and light foreign matter such as leaves or vinyl fragments rises on the surface of the water to easily remove contaminants"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100927631-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "1 to 3, when rainwater is first moved through a manhole or the like and is introduced into the rainwater storage tank 100 through the inlet 120, the relatively heavy contaminants in the sedimentation tank 200 sink and relatively light contaminants accumulate on the surface of the water"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100955909-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in addition, in order to solve the problem that the contaminants accumulated in the inflow tank decay and cause odor after the rainfall is over, the hole is drilled at the bottom of the inflow tank, and gravel or porous media is installed outside to filter the contaminants"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100958442-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "however, the conventional non-point contaminant purification device of the initial excellent excellent outflow water is the final outflow pipe line 21 only after the rainwater received in the median filling tank 13 and the settling tank 14 of the initial excellent purification tank 10 becomes the full water level"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100962546-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in the end region of the drain pipe, it is preferable that a backflow prevention plate is provided to prevent backflow of contaminants in the sediment holding tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100962546-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "thus, the contaminants accumulated on the bottom surface of the sediment holding tank 410 may be prevented from rising to the filter plate accommodating part 160 by riding the drain pipe 420"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100962546-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "thus, particulate contaminants contained in rainwater fall into the sediment holding tank 410 and is confined"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100985170-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in addition, in order to solve the problem that the contaminants accumulated in the inflow tank decay and cause odor after the rainfall is over, the hole is drilled at the bottom of the inflow tank, and gravel or porous media is installed outside to filter the contaminants"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101056650-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "here, the drain valve 158 is frequently opened to remove foreign substances when the rainwater reservoir tank 150 is cleaned or when foreign substances are deposited at the bottom"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101113989-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "therefore, since the tip of the connecting pipe 50 is bent downward so as to be submerged in the rainwater in the sedimentation tank 10, contaminants having a small specific gravity such as oil floating on the water surface may not pass through the connecting pipe 50"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101113989-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the contaminant is finally filtered while passing through the side surface of the ball-type water pipe 43 and discharged into the drain hole 24 at the bottom of the filtration tank 23 connected with the water pipe 43"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101133441-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "as described above, the blocking plate 120 is opened so that the rainwater is drained through the drain 10, and the water tank 131 of the blocking plate opening / closing member 130 is filled with rainwater while the rainwater is drained"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101133441-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "when the blocking plate opening and closing member 130 stops the inflow of rainwater into the rainwater tank 132 after the rain, rainwater is drained into the drain hole 132 formed in the rainwater tank 132 to reduce the amount of rainwater in the rainwater tank 132"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101145104-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "accordingly, an object of the present invention is to provide a block for storing wind and solar power in rain or rain in a storage tank 38 while providing blocks for wind and solar power generation in a roof such as a road or a building"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101154026-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in this way, by collecting the contaminants collected in the container 27 periodically, the inside of the rainwater storage tank 20 can be kept clean, and clogging of the drainage system by the contaminants can be prevented"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101181324-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "therefore, after treating the roadbed sediment and sediment contaminants contained in the sewage of rainy weather has been developed and used to flow into natural rivers or nearby sea, there is a storage tank type treatment device"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101191166-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "therefore, since the ground can support the side plate block, the side pressure of the rain water temporarily stored in the storage tank need not be taken into consideration when installing the side plate block"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101197024-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the rainwater penetration system of the present invention stores rainwater underground and partially penetrates underground to effectively inhibit rainwater leakage during heavy rains, and includes a sedimentation tank for depositing sand and foreign substances in water, and rainwater discharged from the sedimentation tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101202677-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "this, the rainwater introduced into the water collection tank 40 along the raw water inlet pipe 46 may include a contaminant and mud not filtered by the screen filter 20 described above, the bottom of the collecting tank 40 there is an effect of sinking by spraying in the down direction of the sump (40)"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101202895-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in addition, the water quality can be discharged only purified rainwater or clear rainwater has the effect of greatly improving the water quality of the river.1 is a block diagram of a rainwater storage device according to the present invention, 2 is a cross-sectional configuration diagram of a switch and a septic tank and a storage tank showing an initial excellent movement path according to the present invention"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101202895-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "meanwhile, the septic tank 30 has a series of decaying tanks 31, filtration tanks 32, an oxidizing tank 33, and a disinfection tank 34 so that the initial rainwater introduced into the stormwater chamber 210 can be sequentially purified"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101202895-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the initial rainwater introduced into the rainwater toil 210 is introduced into the septic tank 30, and the initial rainwater introduced into the septic tank 30 is a series of decay tanks 31, a filtration tank 32, an oxidation tank 33 and , and is stored in the storage tank 40 in a purified state via the disinfection tank 34"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101206269-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "as such, the prefabricated kit vegetation purification channel 110 is continuously disposed such that the bottom rainwater passages 105 of the neighboring prefabricated blocks 102 and 103 communicate with each other and gradually become lower toward the prefabricated kit rainwater storage tank 170"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101219791-B1", "para_id": "claim_7", "text": "the method of claim 1, non-contaminant purification device characterized in that it further comprises a filtration tank connected to the rain pipe and the rainwater flowing through the flow passage of the rain pipe flows to remove foreign substances piggybacked in rainwater"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101226524-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "10-0938223 is difficult to form a wide enough space for cleaning and maintenance after installation of rainwater storage tank because the stand block located inside the rainwater storage tank is rectangular or square hexahedron shape, side block, when assembling the stand block, the upper block and the lower block, it is difficult to correct construction errors and it is still difficult to solve the lower waterproof problem"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101248434-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "the purpose is to provid