e mixture or water stored in the antifreeze tank 18 or the water tank 21 is selected according to the external ambient temperature"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102545607-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "furthermore, the microorganisms filtered here are collected and stored in a low-temperature container (preferably below 15 c.) to prevent contamination, and then put into a dormant tank at a predetermined speed, for example, a movement speed of 2 m / sec, to dormant microorganism collection and dormancy process ( s90) is preferably further included"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102545607-B1", "para_id": "para_11", "text": "microbial collection and dormancy process (s90) in the microorganism collection and dormancy process (s90), the filtered microorganisms are collected and stored in a low-temperature container (preferably below 15 c.) to prevent contamination, and then put into a dormant tank at a predetermined speed, for example, 2m/sec, for dormant treatment"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102563943-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "and further comprising a freeze protection unit installed in the aeration tank connection pipe of the suction unit, the treated water supply pipe of the suction unit, and the washing water supply pipe of the washing unit to prevent the pipes from freezing and bursting, the freeze protection unit, a temperature sensor installed in the aeration tank connection pipe, the treatment water supply pipe of the suction part, and the washing water supply pipe of the washing part to sense the temperature of the pipe or the external temperature around the pipe"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102701112-B1", "para_id": "claim_7", "text": "in claim 1, the above flow control tank a wheel washing facility including a heater to maintain the water temperature above a certain level to prevent freezing and freezing"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102701112-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "according to one embodiment, the flow control tank may include a heater to maintain a water temperature above a certain level to prevent freezing and freezing"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102701112-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "5, the flow control tank (30) may include a heater (60) to maintain the water temperature above a certain level to prevent freezing and freezing"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102701112-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "at a constant temperature of about 20 c through the heater (60), the water stored in the flow control tank (30) can be prevented from freezing in the winter, and freezing of the submersible pump (40), the flow control tank (30), and the pipes can be prevented"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102707115-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the present invention provides an automatic chlorine injection device for preventing contamination of tap water in a public building water tank, which stores a large amount of chlorine in an automatic chlorine injection device and enables timely injection and replenishment, and also prevents deterioration of chlorine solution due to changes in ambient temperature"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102819243-B1", "para_id": "para_9", "text": "that is, when the temperature falls below the critical temperature in winter (e.g., 0 degrees or 5 degrees, etc.), the fire extinguishing water in the fire extinguishing water tank (20) is circulated along the fire extinguishing pipe (10) to prevent freezing or bursting"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200190678-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "conventionally, in order to prevent freezing of water meters and water pipes in an apartment water tanker or a water meter protection container, many schiropols are built in the water meter and water pipes to prevent freezing in cold weather or cold regions falling below a certain temperature"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200321853-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "when the temperature falls below the freezing point, the built-in electronic temperature control device (2-15) of the pcb board (2-1) detects it and the hot water tank (2- by operating the heater 2-3 and the warm water circulation device 2-21 of 2), the temperature inside the system is increased due to electric heat dissipation, thereby preventing the freezing of the system at the source"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200365284-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the heater 16 then raises the temperature in the water tank 10 under the control of the controller 64 to prevent freezing"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200407276-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the controller 124 determines the water temperature of the cold water tank 101 received from the temperature sensor 128, and controls the operation of the freezing unit to control the operation of the freezing unit 101 water temperature of a level suitable for the user to drink cold water of the cold water tank 101 to fit"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200468890-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "therefore, the user can adjust the temperature controller 32 so that the water (w) heating temperature in the steam tank 10 can be arbitrarily set to be heated, whereby the water (w) appropriately according to the freezing state of the freezing pipe"}, {"pat_id": "US-4784173-A", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "when freezing temperatures are sensed by the bulb, there is an outflow of water from the valve device and an inflow of water from the inlet conduit, thereby preventing freezing of water within the tank"}, {"pat_id": "US-4936114-A", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "sufficient aqueous ice slurry is fed to mixing tank 22 by conduit 54 to keep the temperature of the liquid therein close to, but above, the freezing point so that there is no increase in ice particle formation"}, {"pat_id": "US-5816288-A", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "temperature variations, especially low temperatures below freezing, can cause the screens to frost over and become damaged thus allowing an entrance to the storage tank for insects and other undesired elements"}, {"pat_id": "US-5876596-A", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "after valve 44 has been open for a sufficiently long interval to permit the essentially deuterium free water from separator 28 to flow into tank 50, timer 62 or microprocessor 18 activates cooling element 56 to reduce the temperature of the water sample to the freezing point (32 f.)"}, {"pat_id": "US-6152707-A", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "likewise, a heater 34 may be included inside storage tank 12, to prevent the water stored in tank 12 from freezing in low temperatures"}, {"pat_id": "US-6152707-A", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "a heater may be activated at low water temperatures to prevent the water inside tank 112 from freezing"}, {"pat_id": "US-8141584-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in colder environments, existing exterior collection and storage tanks may crack or break when the temperature drops below freezing, and the water in the tank turns to ice"}, {"pat_id": "US-8141584-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "when the temperature of the water in the storage tank falls below a specified temperature for a specified period of time, thereby indicating that the possibility of freezing exists, the microprocessor activates the pump to dump water from the storage tank through the alternate outlet to the alternate destination"}, {"pat_id": "US-8388833-B2", "para_id": "para_14", "text": "for the top of the tank, a non-illustrated insulated lid (e.g., having an r-12 rating) can cover the entire open top and help keep the temperature regulated and prevent both evaporative cooling and contamination from outside sources"}, {"pat_id": "US-9482357-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in doing so, pressure relief in the system at a temperature above the freezing point of water, generates fluid flow from the well and/or pressure tank or other source, thereby preventing freeze-up"}, {"pat_id": "US-9482357-B2", "para_id": "para_7", "text": "above the freezing point of water, will open and allow relatively warmer water from the tank 304 to enter the trough to prevent ice buildup when the air temperature is cool"}, {"pat_id": "US-9567250-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the preheating coils may contain antifreeze which can be circulated to prevent freezing of the preheat tank when not in use or to maintain the temperature of the preheat tank"}, {"pat_id": "US-9567250-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the antifreeze filled coils may continue to flow to prevent freezing of the preheat tank when not in use or to maintain the temperature of the preheat tank"}]</data>
