  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "JP-5042805-B2", "para_id": "para_21", "text": "specifically, when the water level gauge 111 detects that the water level in the contaminant removal tank 110 is higher than the specified water level, control is performed to relatively increase the amount of water transferred by the advection pump 122, and the contamination level is also increased"}, {"pat_id": "JP-5042805-B2", "para_id": "para_28", "text": "for example, in the case of the water level gauge 111 having a configuration in which an on signal is output when the water level of the contaminant removal tank 110 exceeds a prescribed water level defined in advance and an off signal is outputted when the water level falls below the prescribed water level, the amount of effluent water can be derived from the time when the off signal switches"}, {"pat_id": "JP-6492150-B1", "para_id": "para_7", "text": "that is, the circuit for detecting the conduction between the electrodes due to the water leakage is designed using the circuit for detecting the water level of the water receiving tank conventionally used"}, {"pat_id": "JP-6492150-B1", "para_id": "para_7", "text": "the circuit for detecting the water level in the water receiving tank is a low voltage ac circuit in order to avoid electric shock and prevent electrolysis because the electrodes are always submerged"}, {"pat_id": "KR-0137696-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "moreover, the method of checking the low water level in the water tank by using the air tank is very conventional, and it only functions to block the flow of water only when the water is almost full in the water tank, thereby making it difficult to identify the low water amount in the water tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-0137696-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "moreover, the method of checking the low water level in the water tank by using the air tank is very conventional, and it only functions to block the flow of water only when the water is almost full in the water tank, thereby making it difficult to identify the low water amount in the water tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100314663-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "and water level (36) (37) is provided, the electronic safety valve (e) automatically discharged to the outside when abnormal pressure to maintain the set pressure and to prevent damage and deformation of the tank ( 39) and automatic air discharge valves 34 and 35 are provided"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100331066-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "by equaling the water level in groups, the concrete capacity of decaying tanks is reduced and the simultaneous treatment efficiency is maximized"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100499785-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "the controller 64 is difficult to supply water to the water tank 10 due to a failure of the pump 3a or a blockage of the reverse osmosis filter 7 when the lower limit water level detection signal is input for a predetermined time or more among the water level detection signals sh"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100510269-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "into the flow rate adjustment tank 30 in a state in which the coarse contaminant is filtered and removed while passing through), and when the water level detection sensor 33 of the flow adjustment tank 30 detects the water level, the raw water pump 31 according to the detected signal"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100540762-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "the controller 64 is difficult to supply water to the water tank 10 due to a failure of the pump 3a or a blockage of the reverse osmosis filter 7 when the lower limit water level detection signal is input for a predetermined time or more among the water level detection signals sh"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100540762-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "the controller 64 is difficult to supply water to the water tank 10 due to a failure of the pump 3a or a blockage of the reverse osmosis filter 7 when the lower limit water level detection signal is input for a predetermined time or more among the water level detection signals sh"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100546851-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in the control unit 90, when the second filter material 22a of the second filter tank 20 is blocked and the water level is increased, the water flows back through the overflow pipe 45, and this is applied to the detection signal of the second water level sensor 22b"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100546851-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the control unit 90 is blocked by the second filter material 22a of the second filter tank 20 when the water level is increased, the water flows back through the overflow pipe 45, by the detection signal of the second water level sensor 22b the operation of the inflow pump 70 is stopped"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100644949-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "water purifier automatic drainage method of another embodiment of the present invention, the water level check step of detecting the water level of the water tank to determine the number of water, the step of determining the number of water to be confirmed for a certain time, and if a predetermined number or more is confirmed, drainage of the water tank and opening the valve and draining the water, determining whether the water level is confirmed within a predetermined time, checking the water level when the water level is confirmed, and draining the water by opening the water drain valve of the water tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100644949-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "second, after checking the water level, including the drainage step of opening and draining the drain valve of the water tank, it is possible to automatically adjust the water level to prevent the overflow of the refrigerant tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100644949-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "third, when the water level is confirmed for a predetermined number of times or more, a drainage step of opening and draining the drain valve of the refrigerant tank, determining whether the water level is confirmed within a predetermined time, and a water level checking step of checking the water level when the water level is confirmed as a result, errors due to internal factors can be recognized"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100674176-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "since the second filtration system 40 is relatively small and runs for a long time, it filters out contaminants as much as possible, enters the filtered water into the water level control tank 10 and consequently returns it to the swimming pool"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100720388-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "at this time, the primary electrolysis panel unit 100 is provided with a level sensor 111 for measuring the water level of the brine tank (110a), while opening and closing the solenoid valve 112 in accordance with the set water level to replenish the time a first water level detecting unit 110"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100727599-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the overflow prevention process by the water level adjusting apparatus of the present invention is largely, the first blocking step of first blocking the inflow of raw water into the purified water tank 500 by a mechanical opening and closing structure when the water level of the purified water tank 500 is full"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100823240-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "therefore, when the initial rainwater and sediment contaminants are completely excluded from the initial rainwater treatment facility 1 and the pressure or water level becomes zero, the drain pump 21 receiving the water is driven to operate the water tank 10"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100841664-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "the fifth water level sensor 45 detects an overflow phenomenon that occurs when the water level in the electrolytic cell 30 is increased due to a blockage of the outlet 27a or the like, which is not drained or an increase in inflow from the storage tank 20"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100932027-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in particular, the temporary storage tank of chemicals is formed by double walls of the outer wall and the inner wall so that even if the chemical exceeds the inner wall due to the malfunction of the water level control valve, it is protected by the outer wall as well as between the inner wall and the outer wall, that is, the leak detection sensor installed in the safety space"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100932027-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in particular, the temporary storage tank of chemicals is formed by double walls of the outer wall and the inner wall, so that even if the chemical exceeds the inner wall due to the malfunction of the automatic water level control valve, it is protected by the outer wall, and between the inner wall and the outer wall, that is, a leak detection sensor installed in the safety space"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100958442-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "however, the conventional non-point contaminant purification device of the initial excellent excellent outflow water is the final outflow pipe line 21 only after the rainwater received in the median filling tank 13 and the settling tank 14 of the initial excellent purification tank 10 becomes the full water level"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100985209-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "as a result, the reliability of controlling the water level of the water tank can be improved, and there is an advantage that the control device does not malfunction by another even if an error occurs in any one of the pressure sensor and the angle sensor such as leakage into the water pipe"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100985209-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "for example, when a leak occurs in the water supply pipe 120, even if the water level of the water tank 130 continues to increase, the pressure sensor 140 may sense a low pressure"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100985209-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "by estimating the wide water level range, it is possible to increase the reliability of controlling the water level in the water tank, and also, if an error occurs in either the pressure sensor or the angle sensor, such as leakage into the water pipe, the control device does not malfunction by the other"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100985209-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "by estimating the wide water level range, it is possible to increase the reliability of controlling the water level in the water tank, and also, if an error occurs in either the pressure sensor or the angle sensor, such as leakage into the water pipe, the control device does not malfunction by the other"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100992828-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "when the water level of the wastewater introduced into the water treatment tank 110 rises above the water level detection sensor 200, the water level detection sensor 200 blocks the wastewater inlet 112a to prevent the inflow of wastewater"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101000865-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in addition, when the pressurized water tank reaches the minimum water level, the disk interlocked with the buckle automatically descends to close the flow path of the water cylinder connected to the water supply and drain pipe, thereby blocking the air pressure from leaking to the outside through the water supply and drain pipe"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101000865-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in addition, when the pressurized water tank reaches the minimum water level, the disk interlocked with the buckle automatically descends to close the flow path of the water cylinder connected to the water supply and drain pipe, thereby blocking the air pressure from leaking to the outside through the water supply and drain pipe"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101007019-B1", "para_id": "para_4", "text": "at this time, the third non-power flow control device 15 also operates in the shielding direction due to the water pressure applied as the water level rises in the filtration tank 8"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101045390-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the present invention as described above, the water level sensor detects the amount of manure contained in the manure tank to supply the electrolyte to the manure tank and the electrolysis device in accordance with the amount of manure contained in the manure tank to the manure of the appropriate concentration in the manure tank as it flows into the electrolysis device, there is an effect of uniformly treating the manure in the electrolysis device"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101045390-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "when the water level is increased while the manure is filled in the manure tank 10 as described above, the water level detector 30 installed on the other side of the manure tank 10 detects this and the manure tank 10 and the electrolysis device 40"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101054375-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the fifth water level sensor 45 detects an overflow phenomenon that occurs when the water level in the electrolytic cell 30 is increased due to a blockage of the outlet port 27a or the like, which is not drained or an increase in inflow from the storage tank 20 increases"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101113083-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "in addition, the pump well 46 operates the transfer pump when a certain water level is reached while storing the treated water discharged from the organic material decay reaction tank 40"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101113090-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in addition, the pump well 46 is provided with a transfer pump that operates when the predetermined water level is reached while storing the treated water discharged from the organic material decay reaction tank 40"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101113090-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "in addition, the pump well 46 operates the transfer pump when a certain water level is reached while storing the treated water discharged from the organic material decay reaction tank 40"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101130918-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "therefore, the present invention by installing the filtration device 200 in the position as described above, the contaminants in the water discharged through the drain pipe 120 from the swimming pool to be filtered immediately before passing through the water level control tank (300)"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101202895-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "such a structure is intended to block the inflow of the initial excellent water when the water level of the septic tank 30 reaches the full water level due to the continuous inflow of the initial excellent water level"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101220540-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "that is, when the water level in the pressure tank 314 is increased because the pressurized water does not flow smoothly into the flotation tank 200 due to the blockage of the microbubble injection unit 320, the water level sensor 334 detects the pump 312"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101220540-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "that is, when the water level in the pressure tank 314 is increased because the pressurized water does not flow smoothly into the flotation tank 200 due to the blockage of the microbubble injection unit 320, the water level sensor 334 detects the pump 312"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101272800-B1", "para_id": "claim_6", "text": "the method of claim 1, the compressed air supply means provides a compressed air shock wave to the filtration filter according to the state of the reservoir tank level of the water level detector to eliminate the blockage of the filtration filter, or to provide a compressed air shock wave periodically or occasionally to prevent the blockage of the filtration filter"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101272800-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the compressed air supply means provides a compressed air shock wave to the filtration filter according to the state of the reservoir tank level of the water level detector to eliminate the blockage of the filtration filter, or to provide a compressed air shock wave periodically or occasionally to prevent the blockage of the filtration filter"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101296571-B1", "para_id": "claim_4", "text": "the method of claim 3, the stopper is a water level sensor comprising a leak prevention packing to prevent leakage by contacting the water purification tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101296571-B1", "para_id": "claim_4", "text": "the method of claim 3, the stopper is a water level sensor comprising a leak prevention packing to prevent leakage by contacting the water purification tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101322190-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "therefore, when the purified treatment water from which the contaminants have been removed through the purification treatment water recovery pipe 140 provided in the internal treatment tank 200 of the present invention is recovered, the amount corresponding to the purification treatment water by the water level detection means and the control unit 600"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101383594-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "and according to the variable level screen filter according to the present invention, it is possible to support the variable screen unit in connection with the water tank to improve the durability of the equipment, the deformation of the variable screen unit according to the water level is made more quickly to increase the treatment efficiency of sewage it can be effective"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101388033-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "when the water level of the sewage stored in the tank 30 rises and the height of the buckle member 54 increases, the wire 56b is pulled up by the load of the sensing block 56c and the sensing block 56c is lowered"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101660087-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "as the amount of the treated water w introduced into the treated water storage tank 50 gradually increases during the electrolysis step s30, the water level of the treated water w gradually increases"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101676999-B1", "para_id": "para_6", "text": "therefore, according to the present invention, it is possible to monitor the state of water leakage or foreign matter introduced into the water tank 1 by monitoring the rapid change of the water level and the water quality, thereby enabling cleaner and safer water quality management"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101741449-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "that is, if the operating time of the filtration tank is increased, the flow rate of the flow of the rainwater or the flow rate of the treated water is lowered due to the increase of the amount of contaminants collected in the lcd artificial floating filter media, or the water level of the tank before the rainwater is increased do"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101875497-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "and a control unit for controlling driving of the pressurization pressurizing pump to transport the contaminated water to the land storage tank when the internal water level of the shielding facility is higher than a predetermined reference value, and the inside water level of the shielding facility can be adjusted by being transported in both directions between the storage tank and the polluted water storage tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101875497-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "according to the present invention, a pipeline is installed between the shielding facility of the marine waste treatment plant and the land storage tank, and the polluted water of the shielding facility is transported to the land storage tank by the pipeline, thereby reducing the water level in the shielding facility of the marine waste treatment plant"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101875497-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "according to the present invention, by sensing in real time the water level inside the shielding facility of the marine waste treatment plant and the water level outside the sea surface, the polluted water in the shielding facility is transferred to the landfill tank, it can be surely prevented"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101875497-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "that is, when the sea water purification facility 120 can not process all of the contaminated water even though the internal water level of the shielding facility 110 is higher than a predetermined reference value due to a large difference between heavy rain, heavy rain or tide water, and transports the polluted water to the land-based storage tank 140 through the first pipeline 150"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101875497-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the control unit 180 controls the driving of the pressurization pressurizing pump 170 to bypass the contaminated water to the land storage tank 140 when the internal water level of the shielding facility 110 is higher than a predetermined reference value"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101875497-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "for example, in the case of the domestic west coast, the polluted water is transported to the land-based storage tank 140 through the polluted water storage tank 130, thereby indicating that the internal water level of the shielding facility 110 can be lowered"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102032930-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "4, two or more rectangular (40 50 mm) steel reinforcing rods 26 are installed in the partition wall 22 in the vertical direction to prevent deformation due to the water level difference between the tanks"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102391446-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "specifically, the control device 30 may determine whether filter cleaning is necessary by checking whether the water level in the water tank is equal to or greater than a preset threshold value based on the water level detection information"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102400040-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in addition, the water level of the treated water tank is measured in real time, and when the water level is out of a certain range, the gate valve is selectively opened and closed to block the flow path of the overflow pipe, thereby increasing the overflow height of the treatment tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102525037-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "meanwhile, the pressure tank 100 may be provided with a water level measurement unit (not shown) and a drainage unit 170 for adjusting the water level, and a water level gauge 180 for checking the water level from the outside"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102554668-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "will leak control unit 112 is configured to cause ro pump 450 to stop pumping if empty level switch 350a in tank 350 detects air or a critically low water level"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102783510-B1", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "when the water level of the rainwater storage tank (200) reaches the minimum water level (h2), the agitating unit (500) is driven to form a flow to prevent the decay of the water stored in the rainwater storage tank (200)"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102903436-B1", "para_id": "para_4", "text": "is opened by the bending deformation of the elastic membrane (95), so that the amount of polluted air input through the horizontal passage (14) increases, and when the water level in the water tank (91)"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102903436-B1", "para_id": "para_6", "text": "is opened by the bending deformation of the elastic membrane (95), so that the amount of polluted air introduced through the horizontal channel (14) increases, and when the water level in the water tank (91)"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200145021-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "2 is a block diagram of a water purifier to which the water level deviation preventing device of the purified water tank according to the present invention is applied"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200323476-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "into the flow rate adjustment tank 30 in a state in which the coarse contaminant is filtered and removed while passing through), and when the water level detection sensor 33 of the flow adjustment tank 30 detects the water level, the raw water pump 31 according to the detected signal"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200326076-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "since the second filtration system 40 is relatively small and runs for a long time, it filters out contaminants as much as possible, enters the filtered water into the water level control tank 10 and consequently returns it to the swimming pool"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200328661-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "if the treated water is stored in the backwash tank and the water level falls below a certain level during non-operating, it falls down due to the weight of the stopper 9 to block the flow path of the treated water so that the water in the pump head does not empty"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200332116-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "at this time, when the water tank level is a high water level, the flow of water is blocked by the float 42 and the pressure valve 43, so that the current of the pump motor increases without being stabilized as shown in fig"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200365284-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the controller 64 is difficult to supply water to the water tank 10 due to a failure of the pump 3a or a blockage of the reverse osmosis filter 7 when the lower limit water level detection signal is input for a predetermined time or more among the water level detection signals sh"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200425676-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "when the water level in the water tank 40 reaches a predetermined height, the float 56 serves to block the water inlet pipe 50 while rising upward according to the water level"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200442330-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "more specifically, when the purified water is filled to the water level set in the purified water storage tank (pressure tank), the automatic shut off valve for the water purification system can automatically block the inflow of raw water to the purified water filter due to the pressure"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200454214-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "another object of the present invention is to maintain a constant water level using a float valve and to supply a constant concentration of brine to the electrolysis tank so that sodium hypochlorite is equipped with an automatic valve and a flow sensor to produce a constant concentration of sodium hypochlorite it is to provide a generator"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200454214-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "as such, by maintaining the water level at all times using the float valve 131, the suction pressure of saturated brine can be kept constant, and a constant concentration of salt water can be supplied to the electrolysis tank to produce sodium hypochlorite of a constant concentration"}, {"pat_id": "US-4709723-A", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "during periods of high ground water levels, this leakage enabled additional fluid to flow into the tank to compensate for the increased hydraulic pressure of surrounding ground water and water saturated soil"}, {"pat_id": "US-6627073-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "if the water level in the area on the uppermost stream side in the electrolytic tank is controlled in a predetermined range, as in the claim 16, therefore, it is possible to more reliably prevent the water from leaking from the electrolytic tank"}, {"pat_id": "US-9950935-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the power-off operation, if quickly performed upon a significant rise of the water level, may effectively prevent electrical leakage to peripheral devices even if water flows out of the water tank (31)"}, {"pat_id": "US-9950935-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the power-off operation, if quickly performed upon a significant rise of the water level, may effectively prevent electrical leakage to peripheral devices even if water flows out of the water tank (31)"}]</data>
