e road surface 100 does not directly flow into the filling pipe 52 disposed in the filling section 41a, but settles in the sedimentation section 41b"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102505041-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "thus, the filling pipe 52 is prevented from being clogged by foreign substances remaining in the rainwater flowing into the water collecting channel 41 of the road block 40, so that the filling pipe 52 flows into the water collecting tank 41"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102645553-B1", "para_id": "claim_4", "text": "in claim 1, a leak-free sewage flow rate control device, characterized in that the bottom (12) of the rainwater tank (10) is inclined downward toward the sewage outlet (20) to prevent accumulation of sludge"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102671842-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the pipe 46 is arranged at a certain inclination when connecting the lower end of the drain hole 42c and the upper edge of the water tank 20, which prevents rainwater accumulated in the pair of water receiving blocks 42a and 42b from stagnating"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102747240-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "however, due to the overload problem of the above-described wastewater storage tank (30), it is inevitable to install the above-described frame (61) and rainwater blocking tent (60), which requires a lot of effort and cost"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102747240-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "therefore, even if a rainwater blocking tent (60) and frame (61) are not installed in the car wash section (10) of the car wash, there is an effect of resolving the problem of overload caused by rainwater flowing into the wastewater storage tank (30)"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102747240-B1", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "therefore, to block the inflow of rainwater into the wastewater storage tank (30), the above-described rainwater inflow prevention device (100) is installed in the middle of the wastewater inlet pipe (40)"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102783510-B1", "para_id": "claim_7", "text": "in the first paragraph, in order to prevent the decay of water stored in the above-mentioned rainwater storage tank (200), a stirring unit (500) is installed in the center of the bottom surface of the above-mentioned rainwater storage tank (200) so that a flow is formed"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102783510-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "is driven to form a flow to prevent decay of water stored in the rainwater storage tank (200)"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102783510-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "in order to form a flow for preventing the decay of water stored in the above-mentioned rainwater storage tank (200), it is preferable to further include a bypass pipe (620)"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102783510-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "is driven to form a flow for preventing the decay of water stored in the rainwater storage tank (200)"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102783510-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "of the pump (700), thereby forming a flow for preventing decay of the water stored in the rainwater storage tank (200)"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102783510-B1", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "when the water level of the rainwater storage tank (200) reaches the minimum water level (h2), the agitating unit (500) is driven to form a flow to prevent the decay of the water stored in the rainwater storage tank (200)"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102783510-B1", "para_id": "para_7", "text": "7) in addition, in order to form a flow to prevent the decay of water stored in the rainwater storage tank (200), a bypass pipe (620) may be installed on the opposite edge of the suction pipe (710) to supply water into the interior of the rainwater storage tank (200) by a pump (700)"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102783510-B1", "para_id": "para_7", "text": "the structure of the suction pipe (710) or bypass pipe (620) of the pump (700) forms a flow to prevent the decay of water stored in the rainwater storage tank (200) separately from the agitating unit (500)"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102783510-B1", "para_id": "para_8", "text": "is driven to form a flow to prevent the decay of the water stored in the rainwater storage tank (200)"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102885605-B1", "para_id": "para_6", "text": "is blocked to prevent rainwater from flowing into the pretreatment tank (100)"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200343186-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the rainwater receiver 20, the treatment tank 40, and the first partition wall 50 combine block pieces divided into two upper and lower stages, respectively, to form a partitioned water tank, and the upper and lower two block pieces are formed of a connection pin or a metal"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200343186-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "it is well known that the rainwater receiver 20, the maintenance tank 30, and the treatment tank 40 formed by the combination structure of such block pieces may be rectangular or circular, and the entire block may be formed in one tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200357071-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "road drainage with first flush treatment ability the present invention is to insert a filter filling tank having a filtration treatment function in the conventional rainwater receiver to the road surface drainage treatment device having an initial excellent treatment function that can reliably remove and treat contaminants contained in the road surface drainage"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200414927-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "dropping is placed on the concrete foundation and connected to the bolt nut in the transverse direction and the end wall plate is attached to the column along the rainwater tank block requiring the wall"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200449657-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "however, such a conventional device is designed to directly inject rainwater containing sand, cigarette butts, vinyl and other contaminants into the storage tank and settle it so that no contaminants are removed or secondary pollution by sediment occurs"}]</data>
