upper and lower trench conduits"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101196227-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "a water purification filtration layer (70) formed on the upper and lower trench conduits (50, 60) to remove contaminants in rainwater"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101196227-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "a water purification filtration step formed on the inner surface of the upper and lower trench conduits 50 and 60 to remove contaminants in rainwater"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102053107-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "a bad smell blocking member that prevents the coming offensive odor from dissipating to the outside of the grating, and discharges the rainwater that flows back to the outside of the grating when the rainwater rises in the conduit and the rainwater flows back from the conduit"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102053107-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the rainwater flowing from the outside of the grating 10 flows along the inclined upper surface of each malodor blocking blade 122 and accumulates on the inclined lower upper surface of each malodor blocking blade 122, and each of the malodors when the rainwater accumulated on the inclined lower upper surface of the blocking blade 122 is accumulated by a predetermined amount or more, the respective odor blocking blades are formed such that the lower portion of each odor blocking blade 122 faces the conduit due to the weight of the rainwater"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102053107-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "if the rainwater rises in the conduit due to excessive rain, etc., and the rainwater flows back from the conduit, the rainwater flowing back from the conduit pushes up the inclined upper bottom surface of each odor blocking blade 122"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102399564-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the gate 20 not only collects an appropriate amount of sewage or rainwater by opening and closing the inlet, but also blocks the pressure from being transmitted into the collecting pipe due to the rise of the water level in the conduit during flooding to prevent damage to the collecting pipe"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102399564-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "when it rains, the shutter 30 blocks the exit of the conduit 10 to prevent the odor from spreading to the outside"}, {"pat_id": "US-11560697-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "such scenarios can occur when the sewer conduit has been blocked by detritus, and/or accumulation or buildup around the interior of the drainage pipes which can occur without regular maintenance and monitoring of the sewer drainage lines"}]</data>
