  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "JP-3796706-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "test whether or not there is a difference between the actual water level of the reservoir b28 at the current time and if there is a difference, and the actual water level exceeds the water leakage occurrence level pattern, it is determined that there is water leakage, and the water leakage print water leak occurrence information is issued to the output processing unit 8 and the alarm output processing unit 9"}, {"pat_id": "JP-3796706-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "6, when the actual water level (d) on the leakage monitoring day of the distribution reservoir b28 has changed to the current time, the leakage monitoring calculation processing unit 12 compares the actual water level (d) with the leakage occurrence water level pattern (e)"}, {"pat_id": "JP-4297310-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "[0022] reservoir water level abnormal drop monitoring is intended to detect a sudden drop in the water level of a reservoir due to water leakage due to a distribution pipe accident or a large amount of water discharge due to a fire"}, {"pat_id": "JP-H0641138-Y2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "next, when running water is generated in the pipe 2 due to a leakage accident or the like, it rises above the overflow water level 10 in the water reservoir 8"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100706118-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "due to this replenishment, when the water level in the brine reservoir 5 reaches the upper limit, the electric valve 11 is automatically closed to block the supply of water"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101044802-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "when the water level in the brine reservoir 5 reaches the upper limit due to the water supply and replenishment, the electric valve 11 is automatically closed to block the supply of direct water"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102087796-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "according to one disclosure, in block 102, the sewage water level adjusting apparatus 100 may calculate the rate of increase of the amount of sewage introduced into the first intermediate reservoir and the amount of introduced sewage"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102087796-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "according to one disclosure, in block 103, the sewage water level adjusting apparatus 100 may determine, based on an increase rate of the amount of sewage, whether or not the introduced sewage amount exceeds the sewage storage threshold of the first intermediate reservoir as three levels"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102149596-B1", "para_id": "para_4", "text": "the emergency monitoring terminal (120b) is operated by receiving power from the emergency storage battery (20), and information such as whether the valve is opened or closed, flow rate, hydraulic pressure, water level in each reservoir, leakage, etc"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102683587-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "therefore, it is characterized by controlling and managing the operation of the pump by deriving the most stable and efficient optimal drainage reservoir, water level of the manhole, operating conditions of the pump, inlet pressure, and discharge pressure for each block, reservoir, customer, and manhole"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102683587-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "therefore, the operation of the pump is controlled and managed by deriving the most stable and efficient optimal water level in the reservoir for each block and customer"}]</data>
