  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-100634761-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in addition, when it is determined that the communication state is good, the temperature data of the water tank together with the ambient temperature data (which can determine the possibility of freezing of the water pipe, measured by the temperature sensor) and (if the pump abnormality can be determined) preferably, a current sensor is further provided to control the pump using the current data supplied to the pump"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100901209-B1", "para_id": "claim_5", "text": "a freeze protection driver for intermittently driving a pump to prevent freezing of the water supply pipe when the outside air temperature sensed by the temperature sensor is equal to or less than a reference value"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100901209-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "according to this aspect of the present invention, the water supply control device checks the outside air temperature sensed by the temperature sensor and intermittently drives the pump to prevent freezing of the water supply pipe supplying water to the water tank of the drain"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100901209-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "that is, when the outside air temperature falls below the reference value through the temperature sensor 270, the water supply control device 200 intermittently drives the pump 220 to prevent freezing of the water supply pipe 230"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100901209-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "if the outside air temperature falls below the reference value, the pump control unit 250 controls the operation of the freezing prevention driving unit 254"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100908201-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in the sludge preventing and freezing prevention apparatus of the present invention installed as described above, when the temperature of the water is lower than the predetermined temperature, the water supply pipe 20 is opened by the operation of the high pressure pump 30 while the water supply pipe 10 is opened with the automatic opening and closing valve 50"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101707178-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the present invention also provides a method and system for monitoring the supply of groundwater and the groundwater condition by real-time checking of the groundwater level by measuring the groundwater level, temperature, pollution level and pumping flow rate of the groundwater channel,"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102065694-B1", "para_id": "para_8", "text": "if the temperature measured by the temperature sensor 270 provided in the controller 250 is below a specific temperature, the freezing prevention function is performed in a manner of operating the discharge pump 200 for a specific time at a predetermined specific period"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200415940-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "such a freeze protection method by the circulation pump 90 is electric compared to the freeze protection method that prevents freezing of the water supply line by applying heat when the water supply line falls below a predetermined temperature by winding the entire water supply line applied to a conventional water supply fountain with a heating wire"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200415940-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in addition, since the temperature sensor 80 and the circulation pump 90 are installed in the water supply line 20 of the present invention, the water supply line 20 can be freely prevented from freezing in winter"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200433469-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "control setting part the present invention relates to a simple abnormality of water, and more specifically, when the ambient temperature drops below 0 c and there is a possibility of freezing of water pipes, a water intake pump that drives water from underground pipes and the like is driven for a predetermined time interval"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200433469-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "and a freeze blocker configured to control an operation state of the intake pump according to a preset operating condition for freezing prevention of the water pipe when the outside air temperature is detected below the set temperature"}, {"pat_id": "US-10981818-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the higher wattage and overcapacity of the heating element is preferred to ensure that the chamber temperature is maintained because the air pump would bring in cold air in very cold or freezing weather"}, {"pat_id": "US-12442540-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "after turning on the pump and allowing the hot water to flow through the first set of pipelines in the first loop on the property for the period of time, checking a temperature of all floors of the property to determine if there is a noticeable increase in temperature of a particular floor anywhere on the property"}, {"pat_id": "US-12442540-B1", "para_id": "claim_8", "text": "after turning on the recirculation pump and allowing the hot water to flow through the first set of pipelines in the first loop on the property for the period of time, checking a temperature of all floors of the property to determine if there is a noticeable increase in temperature of a particular floor anywhere on the property"}, {"pat_id": "US-12442540-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "after turning on the pump and allowing the hot water to flow through the first set of pipelines in the first loop on the property for the period of time, the method may include checking a temperature of all floors of the property to determine if there is a noticeable increase in temperature of a particular floor anywhere on the property"}, {"pat_id": "US-12442540-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "after turning on the recirculation pump and allowing the hot water to flow through the first set of pipelines in the first loop on the property for the period of time, checking a temperature of all floors of the property to determine if there is a noticeable increase in temperature of a particular floor anywhere on the property"}, {"pat_id": "US-12442540-B1", "para_id": "par