  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-100912781-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "seventh, since the heating wire is provided on the outer surface of the body of the inlet and the dehydration unit, it is possible to prevent the viscosity rise and freezing of the slurry due to the temperature drop, and thus can be used to operate even in winter"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101050727-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the outer mixing part 2 formed as described above slides in contact with the inner diameter or one side and blocks and opens the cold water inlet 5, the hot water inlet 7, and the normal temperature inlet 6 while passing through the water purifier"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101130759-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "by increasing the temperature of the sewage inlet pipe has the advantage of preventing the freezing of sewage"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101290447-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "if it is carried out, if the freeze-expansive force of the tap water is generated by the fall of the ambient temperature in the winter, it is easily delivered to the airbag 430 through the freeze-expansion force inlet 11 and is absorbed to prevent freezing damage of the water meter"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101351825-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in order to prevent the rainwater from easily evaporating during the rain or to prevent the catchment unit 120 from freezing or freezing by lowering the temperature, the inlet opening and closing part 125 is, for example, the opening and closing slide 125a sliding over the inlet 121"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101720174-B1", "para_id": "para_6", "text": "therefore, water passing through the first inlet 111 is relatively low in temperature immediately before freezing (hereinafter referred to as quot"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200426270-Y1", "para_id": "claim_2", "text": "the method of claim 1, by measuring the temperature of the water by the temperature sensor 5 in the water pipe (p2), when the temperature is less than the set temperature, the inlet valve 7 and the outlet valve 19 for a predetermined time to prevent freezing by circulation of water secondary water purification equipment"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200426270-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "and, the flow sensor to prevent the freezing of the filter and the device by opening the inlet valve 7 and outlet valve 19 for a predetermined time when the temperature sensor (5) located in the water pipe (p2) below a set temperature"}, {"pat_id": "US-10246349-B2", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "however, the salinity of salt water/industrial brine 202 that enters freezing desalination cell/unit enclosure 271 via salt water/industrial brine inlet 275 also has influence on the freezing process (the higher the salt concentration, the lower the necessary freezing temperature to be accomplished)"}, {"pat_id": "US-11325845-B2", "para_id": "para_4", "text": "as shown, in block 6592 a controller may determine a difference between a desired temperature and the source inlet temperature"}, {"pat_id": "US-11352267-B2", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "as shown, in block 6592 a controller may determine a difference between a desired temperature and the source inlet temperature"}, {"pat_id": "US-4784173-A", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "when freezing temperatures are sensed by the bulb, there is an outflow of water from the valve device and an inflow of water from the inlet conduit, thereby preventing freezing of water within the tank"}, {"pat_id": "US-5553637-A", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the second chamber 31 has a primary inlet 34 connected at 35 to the outlet 11 via the supply line section 13a subjected to freezing temperature, i.e., aboveground"}, {"pat_id": "US-9810377-B2", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "it is noted that changes of the temperature of a compressible gas in the modified inlet block 444 may cause the gas to expand or contract, and thereby result in unwanted variances in the flow rate"}, {"pat_id": "US-9810377-B2", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "to avoid such unwanted fluctuations in temperature, the increased surface area, or contact area of the chambers 447 provides a heat exchanger interface between the fluid and the material that forms the modified inlet block 444 and thereby minimize changes in fluid temperature as the fluid moves along the surface of the modified inlet block 444"}, {"pat_id": "US-9810377-B2", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "this heat exchanger interface will help in keeping the temperature of the fluid in the modified inlet block 444 constant during the pressure decay, thereby improving the accuracy of the rate-of-decay measurement by avoiding fluctuations in the rate that may have otherwise been cause by fluctuations in the temperature of the modified inlet block 444"}]</data>
