  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-100992828-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "when the water level of the wastewater introduced into the water treatment tank 110 rises above the water level detection sensor 200, the water level detection sensor 200 blocks the wastewater inlet 112a to prevent the inflow of wastewater"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101258565-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the rainwater introduced into the rainwater chamber 10 is increased in quantity and gradually increased in water level to reach the moving induction plate 300 installed in the sewage inlet 22 and the blocking plate 260"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101323649-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "first, if rainwater is supplied through the inlet 1 of the single finishing block 20, it is stored while maintaining the same water level in the entire pipeline while flowing along the curved pipe"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102008815-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in the above-mentioned patent of the prior art, the opening and closing plate is provided as a buoyancy body to increase the internal water level by the inflow of sewage so that the opening and closing plate rotates to block the manhole inlet to prevent backflow of sewage"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102149596-B1", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "the emergency monitoring terminal has an effect of blocking the rise of the water level when the electronic equipment malfunctions by including a buoyancy type inlet water level meter 150 having a mechanical configuration while sharing a water level meter by electronic sensing together with a constant monitoring terminal"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102399564-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the gate 20 not only collects an appropriate amount of sewage or rainwater by opening and closing the inlet, but also blocks the pressure from being transmitted into the collecting pipe due to the rise of the water level in the conduit during flooding to prevent damage to the collecting pipe"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102683587-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "therefore, it is characterized by controlling and managing the operation of the pump by deriving the most stable and efficient optimal drainage reservoir, water level of the manhole, operating conditions of the pump, inlet pressure, and discharge pressure for each block, reservoir, customer, and manhole"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200425676-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "when the water level in the water tank 40 reaches a predetermined height, the float 56 serves to block the water inlet pipe 50 while rising upward according to the water level"}]</data>
