  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-100485742-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "8a) ( 19) is provided to prevent leakage of rainwater stored in the storm water reservoir into the gap between the blocks 1, 2 as shown in fig"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101013596-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in the block-type stormwater storage tank according to the present invention, an assembling groove is formed on the bottom edge of the four sides of the corner block, the side block and the inner block, which are bounded with the open bottom surface, while the assembling groove is formed on the top surface of the corner block, the side block and the inner block"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101013596-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "according to the block type storm reservoir according to the present invention, the corner block, the side block and the inner block can be easily assembled to the base block, and in particular, in order to increase the height of the storage space, the stacking of the blocks in multiple layers can be easily performed"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101013596-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "meanwhile, in the block type storm reservoir 100 according to an embodiment of the present invention, the horizontal block 124, 134, and 144 penetrates between the corner block 120, the side block 130, and the inner block 140 in several sides from all four sides"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101013596-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "becomes meanwhile, the vertical holes 122, 132, and 142 formed on the upper surface of the corner block 120, the side block 130, and the inner block 140 positioned on the uppermost floor in the final step of installing the block type storm reservoir 100 are separate"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101052857-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in addition, another object of the present invention, because each storm storage block is connected via a fastener and a fastening means, not a wire, it is possible to connect and construct each storm storage block very quickly to significantly shorten the installation time it is to provide an excellent storage tank construction method using the excellent storage tank block and the excellent storage tank and the excellent storage tank block"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101052857-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in addition, the storm storage tank of the present invention, characterized in that the outer periphery surface of the storm storage block is provided with a reinforcement of the closing panel fixed through the fastening means so as to prevent the stored rainwater is discharged to the outside"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101224380-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "however, in the field, problems such as securing convenience of pc block assembly construction, securing structural stability of storm water storage tanks constructed by pc block assembly, problems of leaking through gaps between blocks and removing sludge accumulated inside storm water storage tanks are pointed out"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101224380-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the organic integrity of the floor block, corner wall block, side wall block, column block, ceiling border block, and ceiling block strengthens the overall integrity of the storm storage tank, thereby ensuring structural stability of the storm storage tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101468324-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "10 (a), the third open / close board 40 of the present invention can be shut off passively, so that even when the rain is over in the event of an emergency, the river floods or exceeds the sewage treatment capacity of the sewage end treatment plant , it is possible to block a multiple of the initial storm stored in the reservoir"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101485001-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "that is, the rainwater infiltrated through the permeable press block flows directly into the reservoir 500 through the induction pipe installed under the permeable press block, and the road effluent flowing through the rainwater receiver on the road passes through the filtration tank and then flows into the storage tank 500 after the initial storm has been processed through the storage tank 300"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101485001-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "that is, the rainwater infiltrated through the permeable press block flows directly into the reservoir 500 through the induction pipe installed under the permeable press block, and the road effluent flowing through the rainwater receiver on the road passes through the filtration tank and then flows into the storage tank 500 after the initial storm has been processed through the storage tank 300"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101859056-B1", "para_id": "para_7", "text": "therefore, the storage tank structure for stormwater infiltration and storage according to the present invention can ensure sufficient durability against repetitive vehicle shafts since the storage unit blocks have sufficient strength"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200148426-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "due to this, various flies and mosquitoes inhabited in the sewer pipe are blocked by the blocking plates 6 installed on the outer wall surfaces of the waste collection container 4 of the storm drainage tank 1 for roads, thereby preventing passage"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200343186-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "(7) the maintenance and treatment tanks can be installed in a block block made of concrete, or forcedly installed together with the storm water receiver"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200414927-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "1-a is a top plan view of several storm reservoir block slabs and is stacked (1) where the multiple storm reservoir block slabs meet to become one"}]</data>
