w zone due to guerrilla heavy rain, the upper structure of the catchment manhole is configured to be lifted up to block the inlet of the barrier fastening frame"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200338729-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "on the other hand, if more than a certain amount of sediment accumulated in the bottom of the manhole, the movement of wastewater is blocked, so that smooth drainage is not achieved, and should be removed on a regular basis"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200385529-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in addition, the present invention can greatly reduce the phenomenon that the odor of rainwater pipes are discharged into the manholes because the strainer blocks the manholes"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200403422-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "more specifically, by artificially opening and closing the drain hole formed in the manhole cover by opening the drain hole in the rainy season when you want to discharge the sewage or rain, and smoothly discharged sewage or rain water, and closed in the dry season by preventing the leakage of flies, mosquitoes and other harmful insects, and to prevent odors to achieve a more pleasant environment free of odors and pests"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200416889-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "therefore, the rainwater and sewage that did not flow into the upper portion of the trench cover 31 are diverted to the manhole 20 through the boundary block, so that the rainwater and sewage that do not flow through the trench cover 31 flow into other adjacent areas"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200416889-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "to block the upper portion of the trench cover 31, the drainage is not made smoothly, at this time through the inlet / outlet 12 of the body 11 installed on one side is introduced into the manhole 20 ), so that the inflow of water is prevented from rainwater and sewage"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200449090-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in order to solve this problem, it is a device to prevent the backflow of sewage odors to the manhole, and the rainwater smoothly flows into the sewer pipe, and in the absence of rainwater, it blocks the inlet through which rainwater flows into the atmosphere from the sewer pipe or manhole bucket"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200449230-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "more specifically, the present invention relates to a safety manhole cover for preventing rainwater trapping with a catch preventing part and a slope to prevent safety accidents due to rainwater swelling and rainwater leakage during rainy weather and to prevent accidents caused by footing when a pedestrian is walking"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200449230-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "there was a problem that causes an electric shock accident.in order to solve these problems, the present invention prevents safety accidents due to rainwater swelling and rainwater leakage in rainy weather, and safety manholes for preventing rainwater swelling with a catch preventing part and an inclined part to prevent accidents caused by footfalls when pedestrians walk"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200467574-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "and a backflow prevention part provided to block backflow of sewage and rainwater introduced into and drained from the manhole body"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200467574-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "a backflow prevention buoy provided to block the hollow tube by an upward movement by water pressure when the sewage and rainwater flowing into the manhole body are drained"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200467574-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "and a backflow prevention part provided to block backflow of sewage and rainwater introduced into and drained from the manhole body"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200467574-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "a backflow prevention buoy coupled to the hollow tube to prevent departure, provided to block the hollow tube by water pressure when the sewage and rainwater flowing into the manhole body are drained"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200467574-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the reverse flow prevention unit 130 blocks the reverse flow of sewage and rainwater that flows into the manhole body 110 and is drained, thereby inducing sewage and rainwater flowing into the inflow pipe 110a and the manhole cover 120"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200467574-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "when the hollow tube 132 of the induction part 131 is blocked by the backflow prevention buoy 134, the sewage and rainwater generated from the drain pipe 110b are inflowed through the hollow pipe 132 and the manhole cover 120"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200467574-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the backflow prevention manhole 200 according to another embodiment of the present invention, as shown in figures 4 and 5, the manhole body 210 and the upper part is provided to be opened, coupled to the upper portion of the manhole body 210 the manhole cover 220 and a backflow prevention part 230 provided to block backflow of sewage and rainwater"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200467574-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the reverse flow prevention unit 230 blocks the reverse flow of sewage and rainwater that flows into the manhole body 210 and then drains"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200467574-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "when the hollow pipe 232 of the induction part 231 is blocked by the backflow prevention buoy 234, the sewage and rainwater generated from the drain pipe 210b are passed through the hollow pipe 232 to the inlet pipe 210a and the manhole cover 220"}, {"pat_id": "US-11008747-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "however, as with conventional separate sewer manholes, it should be understood that in exceptional use, such as during heavy rain, flooding and/or blockage, the first chamber may be in liquid communication with the second chamber via the first access port and/or the second access port"}]</data>
