  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-100654756-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "when the amount of sewage flowing into the collecting manhole, that is, when the water level changes, the elevating member blocks all of the drainage holes of the fixing plate, thereby preventing the sewage from flowing back to the road through the collecting manhole"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101996050-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in the above-mentioned prior art patents, the open / close plate is provided as a buoyant body, and when the internal water level is raised by the inflow of sewage, the open / close plate is rotated to block the manhole entrance to prevent the backwashing of sewage"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101996050-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "a backflow preventing plate (70) for blocking an upper and lower space instantaneously as the end portion is brought into close contact with the stopper (51) of the tubular body (50) while rotating at a predetermined angle according to the water level flowing into the manhole body (10)"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102008815-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in the above-mentioned patent of the prior art, the opening and closing plate is provided as a buoyancy body to increase the internal water level by the inflow of sewage so that the opening and closing plate rotates to block the manhole inlet to prevent backflow of sewage"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102008815-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "a backflow prevention plate 70 which allows the upper and lower spaces to be blocked at the moment when the end is in close contact with the stopper 51 of the tubular body 50 while rotating at a predetermined angle according to the water level flowing into the manhole body 10"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102683587-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "therefore, it is characterized by controlling and managing the operation of the pump by deriving the most stable and efficient optimal drainage reservoir, water level of the manhole, operating conditions of the pump, inlet pressure, and discharge pressure for each block, reservoir, customer, and manhole"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200351993-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "however, when the water level of the sewage collected in the manhole is increased due to excessive sewage or heavy rain in the manhole, the level of the sewage is increased and the cover blocking the discharge hole rises due to the sewage level so that the slope is forcibly opened"}]</data>
