  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-100614766-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "the contaminants are adsorbed in the precipitated sand or mud, and as a result, the precipitates absorbing the contaminants are formed in the mud state at the bottom and the vicinity of the storm receiver 10 and the discharge box 91"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100614766-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "(3) since the filter filling tank which removes contaminants contained in the drainage by filtration or adsorption is detachably installed in the treatment tank, while the drainage flowed from the inlet of the storm receiver flows through the treatment tank, contaminants contained in the waste water are removed by the filter medium"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100750645-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the present invention relates to a multifunctional storm receiver that can reliably filter oily contaminants and prevent odors in the confluence area"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100750645-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "these storm receivers store the road drainage during rainfall and transfer it to the filtration apparatus to adsorb and remove contaminants contained in the road drainage, and then discharge only the treated water to the sewer"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101250076-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the road surface storm water treatment tank 123a is provided with an inflow chamber 123a3, a processing chamber 123a4, and an outflow chamber 123a5, and the inflow chamber 123a3 has a contaminant receiver 123b and a processing chamber ( 123a4) is provided with pollutant filtration / adsorption means 123c, respectively"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101280771-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the storm flows into the inlet chamber 123a3 and the contaminants are removed by the obstacle receiver 123b during the passage through the inlet chamber 123a3"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200343186-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "as a result, deposits absorbing contaminants are deposited in the mud at the bottom of the storm receiver 20, the maintenance tank 30, and the treatment tank 40"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200343186-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "then, after the rainfall flows into the storm receiver 20, it is re-introduced into the maintenance tank 30, the treatment tank 40 is to properly remove the contaminants in the treatment tank 40"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200343186-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "on the other hand, if the removal process of the contaminants continues, the bottom of the storm receiver 20, the maintenance tank 30 and the treatment tank 40, deposits containing contaminants are deposited, and the filter medium filling tank ( 70) contaminants will also collect inside, and regular removal will be required"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200343186-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "(6) the bottom of the storm receiver, maintenance tank and treatment tank is laminated with synthetic resin sheet, treatment media and porous sheet made of permeable material so that the road drainage remaining in the drainage system is allowed to penetrate into the soil with contaminants removed"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200357071-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the contaminants are adsorbed in the precipitated sand or mud, and as a result, the precipitates absorbing the contaminants are formed in the mud state at the bottom and the vicinity of the storm receiver 10 and the discharge box 91"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200357071-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "(3) since the filter filling tank which removes contaminants contained in the drainage by filtration or adsorption is detachably installed in the treatment tank, while the drainage flowed from the inlet of the storm receiver flows through the treatment tank, contaminants contained in the waste water are removed by the filter medium"}]</data>
</edge>
