  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-100614766-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "(3) since the filter filling tank which removes contaminants contained in the drainage by filtration or adsorption is detachably installed in the treatment tank, while the drainage flowed from the inlet of the storm receiver flows through the treatment tank, contaminants contained in the waste water are removed by the filter medium"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100633532-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in addition, if rainwater and sewage flowing into the rainwater receiver 51 contain foreign matters, the rainwater and sewage introduced into the lower portion due to the foreign matters are blocked, and the rainwater and sewage are not drained"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100750645-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "these storm receivers store the road drainage during rainfall and transfer it to the filtration apparatus to adsorb and remove contaminants contained in the road drainage, and then discharge only the treated water to the sewer"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100975670-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "1 is a perspective view of a rain barrier for a waste block according to the present invention, figure 2 is an exploded perspective view of the rain barrier for waste block according to the present invention, figure 3 is a cross-sectional view of the rain barrier for waste block according to the present invention, 4 is a cross-sectional view of another type of garbage collection rain receiver according to the present invention, fig"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100975670-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "figure 4 is a cross-sectional view of another type of garbage blocking rain receiver according to the present invention"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100975670-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "figure 6 is a cross-sectional view of another type of garbage blocking rain receiver according to the present invention"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101054283-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the earth and sand receivers may be in contact with the blocking member along the outer edge of the upper portion to block foreign matter contained in the rainwater and sewage flowing through the cover between the manhole inner wall and the earth and sand receiver"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101167604-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "since the connection pipe p1 can be inclined, the drain port 115 provided in the rainwater receiver can be conveniently connected to the connection fume pipe (drain pipe), thereby preventing leakage at the connection portion"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101193342-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in order to prevent the water outlet pipe 3 from being blocked by foreign substances introduced with rainwater, the rainwater receiver of this structure has a certain distance from the bottom of the pipeline so that the foreign matter is accumulated in a wet state at all times"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101250076-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "rainwater is introduced into the inflow chamber 123a3 and the contaminants are removed by the debris receiver 123b during the process of passing through the inflow chamber 123a3"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101632920-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "it is another object of the present invention to provide a malodor leakage prevention device capable of smoothly performing an excellent discharge operation and an odor shielding function by ensuring stability of operation and a rainwater receiver equipped with the same"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101632920-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in order to attain the above object, the malodor leakage prevention device according to the present invention is a malodor leakage prevention device installed in a rainwater receiver, comprising"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101632920-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in order to attain the above object, the malodor leakage prevention device according to the present invention is a malodor leakage prevention device installed in a rainwater receiver, comprising"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101632920-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in order to attain the above object, the malodor leakage prevention device according to the present invention is a malodor leakage prevention device installed in a rainwater receiver, comprising"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101632920-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "and a malodor leakage prevention device installed inside the rainwater receiver housing"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101632920-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "meanwhile, the malodor leakage prevention device (v) according to the present invention can be constructed by directly installing the shield plate (2) having the above-described structure on the rainwater receiver housing, and a sub housing (1)"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101632920-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "5a and 5b, the rainwater collector having the malodor leakage prevention device includes a rainwater receiver enclosure 6 having a drainage passage formed therein, and a plurality of fine inflow holes formed on the rainwater receiver enclosure 6 a rainwater catching cover 7, and a malodor leakage preventing device v installed in the rainwater catching enclosure 6"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101632920-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "hereinafter, the malodor leakage prevention device according to the first embodiment of the present invention and the operation of the rainwater receiver having the same will be briefly described"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101632920-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "thereafter, the odor leakage preventing device (v) is joined to the lower housing part (62) of the rainwater receiver by welding or the like to complete the rainwater receiver, and then the windwater is installed at the edge of the road or the sidewalk, the cover 7 is installed"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101654689-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "at this time, due to the self weight of the rainwater receiver cover member 2, the seat back protrusion 42 is pressed, so that the filter block 1 is firmly fixed and supported"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101715262-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "however, there has recently been a problem in that leaks occur in the rainwater harbor connection port to weaken the ground where the rainwater receiver is installed, and furthermore, there is a problem that the sinkhole is formed due to the leakage of the earthworm"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101715262-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "thirdly, there is an advantage that the sinking of the ground caused by the rainwater receiver can be prevented by leakage of the rainwater due to the mortar operation finishing of the joint between the rainwater collector and the connecting pipe"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102561269-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "a foreign material inflow prevention net installed to cover the upper part of the rainwater collecting receiver to prevent the inlet hole from being blocked by foreign substances accumulated on the upper surface of the rainwater collecting receiver"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200167095-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "therefore, the sewage receiver was installed when the hydraulic pressure acted to block the odor, and when the hydraulic pressure was removed, there was a damper of a structure that automatically shuts off the drain by self-weight or spring force"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200343186-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the rainwater receiver 20, the treatment tank 40, and the first partition wall 50 combine block pieces divided into two upper and lower stages, respectively, to form a partitioned water tank, and the upper and lower two block pieces are formed of a connection pin or a metal"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200343186-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "it is well known that the rainwater receiver 20, the maintenance tank 30, and the treatment tank 40 formed by the combination structure of such block pieces may be rectangular or circular, and the entire block may be formed in one tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200343186-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "then, after the rainfall flows into the storm receiver 20, it is re-introduced into the maintenance tank 30, the treatment tank 40 is to properly remove the contaminants in the treatment tank 40"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200343186-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "(6) the bottom of the storm receiver, maintenance tank and treatment tank is laminated with synthetic resin sheet, treatment media and porous sheet made of permeable material so that the road drainage remaining in the drainage system is allowed to penetrate into the soil with contaminants removed"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200357071-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "road drainage with first flush treatment ability the present invention is to insert a filter filling tank having a filtration treatment function in the conventional rainwater receiver to the road surface drainage treatment device having an initial excellent treatment function that can reliably remove and treat contaminants contained in the road surface drainage"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200357071-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "(3) since the filter filling tank which removes contaminants contained in the drainage by filtration or adsorption is detachably installed in the treatment tank, while the drainage flowed from the inlet of the storm receiver flows through the treatment tank, contaminants contained in the waste water are removed by the filter medium"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200361466-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "bad smell intercepting apparatus of rain and dirty water receiver the present invention relates to a malodor blocking device of a rainwater receiver, and more particularly, to increase the water level and to increase the water level at the discharge end of the openable malodor blocking device such that the water pressure pushes the opening door"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200361466-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "it has been disclosed that the odor blocking device of the rainwater receiver has a long oval structure so that sludge components contained in rainwater or sewage do not accumulate in the discharge end of the valve body"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200361466-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "to increase the open and close the door smoothly, and even if the water flows little by little to provide a odor blocking device of the rainwater receiver to open and close the door smoothly by the water pressure in the inclined portion of the discharge end"}]</data>
