  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-101193342-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in order to prevent the water outlet pipe 3 from being blocked by foreign substances introduced with rainwater, the rainwater receiver of this structure has a certain distance from the bottom of the pipeline so that the foreign matter is accumulated in a wet state at all times"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101323649-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "first, if rainwater is supplied through the inlet 1 of the single finishing block 20, it is stored while maintaining the same water level in the entire pipeline while flowing along the curved pipe"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101323649-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "rainwater is discharged to the outside through the outlet (2) of the single closing block 20 located in the other end of the pipeline while the rainwater flows through the pipeline as in the supply process"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102053107-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "as described above, as the manhole malodor prevention device 100 includes the malodor preventing casing member 110 and the malodor blocking member 120, the malodor in the pipeline is prevented from flowing back and the rainwater is prevented"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102053107-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "on the other hand, while the rain odor blocking member 320 maintains the closed state, when the rainwater rises in the pipeline due to excessive rain, such as rainy season, the rainwater flows back from the pipeline, the water level in the pipeline rises"}]</data>
