  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-101238623-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "a drop in temperature or pressure in the zone may prevent rapid freezing of residual moisture or air itself in the pipeline"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101244452-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "by arranging a water temperature sensor and a heater for directly heating the fire water in the pipeline, it is possible to efficiently prevent freezing of the pipeline of the fire fighting apparatus"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101244452-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the heater unit 600 serves to prevent damage to the pipeline 510 due to volume expansion caused by freezing and freezing of the fire fighting water in the pipeline 510 due to the influence of low temperature in the winter season"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101244452-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "on the other hand, both the heater unit 600 and the water temperature detection unit 700 to prevent the fire water provided in the pipeline 510 is frozen in the winter and freezing may be disposed inside the fire box (530)"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101244452-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the heater unit 600 and the water temperature detection unit 700 are both electrically connected to the control unit 800, and when the temperature of the fire water in the pipeline 510 sensed by the water temperature detection unit 700 is below the freezing point, the control unit 800 ) provides power to the heater unit 600 to directly supply heat to the fire water in the pipeline 510 to prevent freezing by freezing of the pipeline 510"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101244452-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the heater unit 600 and the water temperature detection unit 700 are both electrically connected to the control unit 800, and when the temperature of the fire water in the pipeline 510 sensed by the water temperature detection unit 700 is below the freezing point, the control unit 800 ) provides power to the heater unit 600 to directly supply heat to the fire hydrant 540 and the fire fighting water in the conduit 510 to prevent freezing due to freezing of the conduit 510"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101244452-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "as described in detail above, in order to prevent the pipeline from which fire water is discharged from a fire hydrant, a hose reel, a fire truck, etc., freezing and freezing in the winter, the water temperature is detected in direct contact with the fire water in a pipeline such as a fire hydrant, a hose reel, or a fire truck"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101762614-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "these ducts are subject to cracking due to contraction and expansion due to external environment such as corrosion, external shock, temperature, etc., resulting in problems such as leakage of the fluid flowing in the pipeline to the outside or severance of pipeline do"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101762614-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "these ducts are subject to cracking due to contraction and expansion due to external environment such as corrosion, external shock, temperature, etc., resulting in problems such as leakage of the fluid flowing in the pipeline to the outside or severance of pipeline do"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101910492-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "these ducts are subject to cracking due to contraction and expansion due to external environment such as corrosion, external shock, temperature, etc., resulting in problems such as leakage of the fluid flowing in the pipeline to the outside or severance of pipeline do"}, {"pat_id": "US-10215341-B2", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "pressure, flow rates, temperature, etc.), pipeline fluid sampling/testing/monitoring data, pipeline condition data, leak detection data, system 10 component data, or a combination thereof"}, {"pat_id": "US-10634284-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "using the latent heat signatures associated with phase changes of a process fluid (in this case sulphur) to identify solidification or melting of the process fluid at locations along a pipeline is not dependent on a particular melting or freezing temperature"}, {"pat_id": "US-10634284-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "for example, curves in the pipeline may tend to accumulate more solidified process fluid compared to straight sections of the pipeline, and anchor points along the pipeline may accumulate more solidified process fluid as a result of heat transfer to the anchors supporting the pipeline, which may drop the temperature of the anchor points below the freezing point of the process fluid"}, {"pat_id": "US-10704740-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "this drop in temperature may mimic the thermal change caused by a leak in the pipeline"}, {"pat_id": "US-11112190-B2", "para_id": "claim_18", "text": "wherein inhibiting heat transfer is in response to an external temperature being less than a threshold temperature, and wherein placing a heat-transfer material layer of the ptd in contact with the pipeline to provide for heat transfer from the environment through the heat-transfer material layer to the pipeline is in response to the external temperature exceeding the threshold temperature"}, {"pat_id": "US-11112190-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the pcm moves the heat-transfer layer into contact with the pipeline via thermal expansion of the pcm in response to the external temperature exceeding the threshold"}, {"pat_id": "US-11112190-B2", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "(or a different temperature for a different application), the expansion of the pcm bag 428 and the right and left pet blocks 414a, 414b is not sufficient to cause the graphene sheet 408 to become in contact with the pipeline 402"}, {"pat_id": "US-11112190-B2", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "(or a different temperature for a different application), the expansion of the pcm bag 428 and the right and left pet blocks 414a, 414b is not sufficient to cause the graphene sheet 408 to become in contact with the pipeline 402"}, {"pat_id": "US-11112190-B2", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "at block 1806, the method includes affecting the temperature of the transported fluid in the pipeline"}, {"pat_id": "US-11112190-B2", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "the inhibiting of heat transfer (block 1802) from the pipeline to the environment (e.g., when the external temperature is below a threshold) may maintain the temperature of the fluid in the pipeline"}, {"pat_id": "US-11112190-B2", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "the promoting of heat transfer (block 1804) from the environment to the pipeline (e.g., when the external temperature is above a threshold) may increase the temperature of the fluid in the pipeline"}, {"pat_id": "US-11112190-B2", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "the placing of the heat-transfer material layer of the ptd in contact with the pipeline to provide for heat transfer from the environment through the heat-transfer material layer to the pipeline may be in response to the external temperature exceeding the threshold temperature"}, {"pat_id": "US-11112190-B2", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "the control material may move the graphene layer into contact with the pipeline via thermal expansion of the control material in response to an external temperature exceeding a threshold"}, {"pat_id": "US-11112190-B2", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "the left section and the right section may exert compression on the control material to facilitate movement of the graphene layer in the gap into contact with the pipeline in response to an external temperature exceeding a threshold"}, {"pat_id": "US-11112190-B2", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "the pcm (e.g., pcm bag) moves the heat-transfer layer into contact with the pipeline via thermal expansion of the pcm in response to the external temperature exceeding the threshold"}, {"pat_id": "US-11193847-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "thus, in such embodiments, based on the sensor data determined by the temperature sensors 52, the control sub-system 54 may determine fluid temperature at multiple different locations along the bore in the pipeline system 10 (process block 106)"}, {"pat_id": "US-11199502-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "it is very easy to produce the natural gas hydrate in the oil and gas exploitation and transportation process especially in low-temperature and high-pressure deep water environments, and the natural gas hydrate will block a conveying pipeline"}, {"pat_id": "US-12111007-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "a conventional leak detection system is based on several models, which provide continuous monitoring of pressures, temperatures, and flow at some points along the pipeline with automated analysis"}, {"pat_id": "US-12235188-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "by integrating on-site pressure sensing and temperature sensing, operating state monitoring on the heating pipelines and pipeline leakage analysis and early warning are realized without adding sensing devices"}, {"pat_id": "US-12235188-B2", "para_id": "para_43", "text": "at the moment of leakage, the temperature of the inner surface of the thermal insulation layer 6 is the temperature of the outer wall of the pipeline without leakage, that is ton=tol, and thus, the variation of the transient heat capacity of steam at the moment of leakage can be obtained by substituting tol into the formula (1) \u03b4q"}, {"pat_id": "US-12235188-B2", "para_id": "para_46", "text": "and the variation of the temperature in the pipeline is less affected by an external environment, the process of solving the transient pressure by the leakage transient temperature is specifically as follows"}, {"pat_id": "US-12235188-B2", "para_id": "para_62", "text": "because collection analysis of the pressure sensors on the pressure waves are mature, and the variation of the transient temperature at the leakage point can be hardly embodied by data collected by the temperature sensors, a pipeline leakage early warning is realized by setting a pressure threshold value"}, {"pat_id": "US-12265759-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in the daily construction process of heating pipelines, there will be problems such as pipeline leakage, but generally, the pipeline is tested manually on a regular basis to ensure the normal operation of the pipeline, or after receiving complaints from users, it may be because individual users can t receive the heating or the heating temperature is too low, so the pipeline detection will be carried out"}, {"pat_id": "US-12442540-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "after turning on the pump and allowing the hot water to flow through the first set of pipelines in the first loop on the property for the period of time, checking a temperature of all floors of the property to determine if there is a noticeable increase in temperature of a particular floor anywhere on the property"}, {"pat_id": "US-12442540-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "if the noticeable increase in the temperature of the particular floor anywhere on the property is detected, determining that the detectable underground cold water pipeline containing the leak is located beneath or near the particular floor"}, {"pat_id": "US-12442540-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "if the noticeable increase in the temperature is detected, marking the particular floor associated with the noticeable increase in the temperature on the property as the area of the property to be used to access the detectable underground cold water pipeline containing the leak for any future repair or replacement of the detectable underground cold water pipeline"}, {"pat_id": "US-12442540-B1", "para_id": "claim_8", "text": "after turning on the recirculation pump and allowing the hot water to flow through the first set of pipelines in the first loop on the property for the period of time, checking a temperature of all floors of the property to determine if there is a noticeable increase in temperature of a particular floor anywhere on the property"}, {"pat_id": "US-12442540-B1", "para_id": "claim_8", "text": "if the noticeable increase in the temperature of the particular floor anywhere on the property is detected, determining that the detectable underground cold water pipeline containing the leak is located beneath or near the particular floor"}, {"pat_id": "US-12442540-B1", "para_id": "claim_8", "text": "if the noticeable increase in the temperature is detected, marking the particular floor associated with the noticeable increase in the temperature on the property as the area of the property to be used to access the detectable underground cold water pipeline containing the leak for any future repair or replacement of the detectable underground cold water pipeline"}, {"pat_id": "US-12442540-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "after turning on the pump and allowing the hot water to flow through the first set of pipelines in the first loop on the property for the period of time, the method may include checking a temperature of all floors of the property to determine if there is a noticeable increase in temperature of a particular floor anywhere on the property"}, {"pat_id": "US-12442540-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the method may further include determining that the detectable underground cold water pipeline containing the leak is located beneath or near the particular floor if the noticeable increase in the temperature of the particular floor anywhere on the property is detected"}, {"pat_id": "US-12442540-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "after turning on the recirculation pump and allowing the hot water to flow through the first set of pipelines in the first loop on the property for the period of time, checking a temperature of all floors of the property to determine if there is a noticeable increase in temperature of a particular floor anywhere on the property"}, {"pat_id": "US-12442540-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "if the noticeable increase in the temperature of the particular floor anywhere on the property is detected, the method includes determining that the detectable underground cold water pipeline containing the leak is located beneath or near the particular floor"}, {"pat_id": "US-12442540-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "6 is a pictorial illustration of an exemplary manifold having multiple pipelines on which a cold-water temperature test is performed to identify a leak"}, {"pat_id": "US-12442540-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "7 is a pictorial illustration of an exemplary manifold having multiple pipelines on which a cold-water temperature test is performed to identify a leak"}, {"pat_id": "US-12442540-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "either way as the user 102 performs temperature tests throughout the manifolds 112 and uses fixtures 122 selectively the user 102 can determine which pipelines 112 connect to the leaking pipe and have a leak 154"}, {"pat_id": "US-12442540-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "1) determining whether the leak is on the a cold side or a hot side 2) identifying a first test manifold 112 and identifying a first fixture 122 associated with that first test manifold 112 3) changing the temperature of the pipelines 114 of the first test manifold 112 (i.e"}, {"pat_id": "US-12442540-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "so, after determining that the manifold 112 is before or after the leak 154, to determine which pipelines 114 are feedlines 116 or distribution lines 118, the user 102 has to perform another time temperature test with the fixture 122 turned on"}, {"pat_id": "US-12442540-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "by performing time based temperature checks, the user 102 may determine that pipeline 114c has water flowing down towards the leak 154 at the main water entrance 108 to the property 104 and through pipeline 114c"}, {"pat_id": "US-12442540-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in order for the user to determine where a distribution line 118 that has water flowing through the distribution line 118 to get to the leak 154 is going, the user 102 has to temperature check each pipeline 114a-114c of the manifold 112a and compare the results one by one with each fixture 122 present on the property 104"}, {"pat_id": "US-12442540-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "accordingly, the user 102 can temperature test the pipelines 114 of all of the manifolds 112 for the half bath vanity sink 842, the half bath toilet 840, hose bib 1 810, and hose bib 2 812 to see if the leak 154 is before or after each manifold 112 of each fixture 112 and to identify point a 170 and point b 172"}, {"pat_id": "US-12442540-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "after opening up at these areas and performing temperature checks, the user 102 tries to determine 1) if the leak 154 is past or before said manifold 112 2) which one pipeline 114 is the feedline 116 and which pipeline(s) 114 are the distribution lines 118 and 3) which pipelines 114 in each manifold 112 take water to other fixtures 122 on the property 104"}, {"pat_id": "US-12442540-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "after performing this initial temperature test, the user 102 knows that pipeline 114c is a distribution line 118 and is most likely the pipeline 114 leading to the leak 154 because of the temperature change"}, {"pat_id": "US-12442540-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "11-18, because the hot water will be leaking out through the underground leaking cold water pipeline 126 containing an underground leak 154 which will make the surrounding area around the underground leaking cold water pipeline 126 and floors above the underground leaking cold water pipeline 126 noticeably warmer via touch 142 or temperature testing equipment 144"}, {"pat_id": "US-12442540-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "at step 1612, if the noticeable increase in the temperature of the particular floor anywhere on the property is detected, the user 102 may safely assume and determine that the detectable underground cold water pipeline 114 containing the leak 154 is located beneath or near the particular floor"}, {"pat_id": "US-12442540-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "at step 1712, after turning on the recirculation pump 180 and allowing the hot water to flow through the first set of pipelines 114 in the first loop on the property 104 for the period of time, checking a temperature of all floors of the property 104 to determine if there is a noticeable increase in temperature of a particular floor anywhere on the property 104"}, {"pat_id": "US-12442540-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "at step 1714, if the noticeable increase in the temperature of the particular floor anywhere on the property 104 is detected, the method includes determining that the detectable underground cold water pipeline 114 containing the leak 154 is located beneath or near the particular floor"}, {"pat_id": "US-12442540-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "at step 1812, the method includes checking a temperature of all floors of the property 104 to determine if there is a noticeable increase in temperature of a particular floor anywhere on the property 104 after turning on the pump 180 and allowing the hot water to flow through the first set of pipelines 114 in the first loop on the property 104 for the period of time"}, {"pat_id": "US-12442540-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "at step 1814, if the noticeable increase in the temperature of the particular floor anywhere on the property 104 is detected, the method includes determining that the detectable underground cold water pipeline 126 containing the leak 154 is located beneath or near the particular floor"}, {"pat_id": "US-3978709-A", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "description of the invention this invention relates to a method and a system for detecting a leakage from a liquid-transporting pipeline, and more particularly to a method and a system for minimizing a pressure change due to a temperature change of a liquid within a blocked pipeline containing the liquid to be transported, and detecting a leakage of the liquid from the blocked pipeline"}, {"pat_id": "US-3978709-A", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "description of the invention this invention relates to a method and a system for detecting a leakage from a liquid-transporting pipeline, and more particularly to a method and a system for minimizing a pressure change due to a temperature change of a liquid within a blocked pipeline containing the liquid to be transported, and detecting a leakage of the liquid from the blocked pipeline"}, {"pat_id": "US-3978709-A", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "however, in the case of larger and longer pipeline, an amount of the liquid to be passed through a flow rate meter will be increased owing to an increase in volume change due to a change in the liquid temperature in the pipeline, and the sensitivity of the flow rate meter is lowered for a small amount of leakage"}, {"pat_id": "US-3978709-A", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "therefore, it is necessary to make the block distance shorter than a specified length, e.g., said 10 km, or to wait for the leakage detection until the temperature of the pipeline has reached the ambient one, for reducing the effect of the temperature change"}, {"pat_id": "US-3978709-A", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "therefore, it is necessary to make the block distance shorter than a specified length, e.g., said 10 km, or to wait for the leakage detection until the temperature of the pipeline has reached the ambient one, for reducing the effect of the temperature change"}, {"pat_id": "US-6530263-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "as another example, prior art methods and apparati for detecting and locating a fluid leak in underground fluid conveying conduits typically fail to compensate for variances in the ambient temperature, thereby compromising the accuracy of the calculation of the location of the source of leaks in the pipeline, which is highly undesirable"}, {"pat_id": "US-6970808-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in choosing the optimum model, a leak detection system that provides continuous monitoring of pressures, temperatures, and flow at points along the pipeline, supported by automated analysis of the data is most ideal"}, {"pat_id": "US-8117998-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "it is possible to prevent pipelines from freezing and bursting at temperatures below zero during the winter, using the configuration of the hot water supplying system 20"}, {"pat_id": "US-8502687-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the determination module 302 determines the pipeline 100 works normally upon the condition that the fluid temperatures falls out of an allowable range or the leaks occur to the pipeline 100"}, {"pat_id": "US-9254221-B2", "para_id": "para_4", "text": "because the role of the heating pipe, the temperature of the liquid in the pipeline will be elevated, and it has an advantage of comfortable and healthy to dispose the pipeline on the pad, it can prevent the leakage, and obtains higher safety"}]</data>
</edge>
